window.IELTS_TOPIC={"topic":13,"en":"Evolution, Genetics & Animal Behaviour","zh":"演化、遺傳與動物行為","items":[{"w":"evolution","pos":"n.","def":"slow change in living things over many generations","cn":"演化","s":"Our biology teacher showed us fossils of early horses, and she explained how ________ slowly changed their size and teeth over millions of years.","zh":"我們的生物老師給我們看早期馬的化石，並解釋了演化如何在數百萬年間慢慢改變牠們的體型和牙齒。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A1","t":"演化"},{"w":"natural selection","pos":"n.phr.","def":"process where living things best suited to their surroundings survive","cn":"天擇","s":"Rabbits with white fur are harder for foxes to see in the snow, so ______ ______ helps them survive and pass on that colour.","zh":"白色毛皮的兔子在雪地裡較不容易被狐狸看見，所以天擇幫助牠們存活並把這種毛色傳下去。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A2","t":"天擇"},{"w":"sexual selection","pos":"n.phr.","def":"choosing mates by features such as bright colours or songs","cn":"性擇","s":"Female birds often choose males with the brightest feathers, and scientists believe ______ ______ explains why many male birds look so colourful.","zh":"雌鳥常常選擇羽毛最鮮豔的雄鳥，而科學家相信性擇解釋了為什麼許多雄鳥看起來如此色彩繽紛。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A3","t":"性擇"},{"w":"artificial selection","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when humans choose which plants or animals breed","cn":"人擇；人工選擇","s":"All the different dog breeds came from wolves, but they look so different because people used ______ ______ for thousands of years.","zh":"所有不同的狗品種都來自狼，但牠們看起來如此不同，是因為人們數千年來一直進行人擇。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A4","t":"人擇"},{"w":"fitness","pos":"n.","def":"how well a living thing survives and has young","cn":"適存度","s":"In biology, ________ does not mean going to the gym, because it describes how many healthy young an animal can produce.","zh":"在生物學中，適存度並不是指去健身房，因為它描述的是一隻動物能產下多少健康的後代。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A5","t":"適存度"},{"w":"common ancestor","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an earlier species that two later species both came from","cn":"共同祖先","s":"Humans and chimpanzees look different today, but scientists say we shared a ______ ______ that lived about six million years ago.","zh":"人類和黑猩猩今天看起來不同，但科學家說我們有一個大約生活在六百萬年前的共同祖先。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A6","t":"共同祖先"},{"w":"speciation","pos":"n.","def":"the forming of a new and separate species","cn":"物種形成","s":"When a river split one group of beetles into two, the groups stopped meeting, and over time ________ produced two different kinds.","zh":"當一條河把一群甲蟲分成兩群後，兩群不再相遇，經過一段時間，物種形成產生了兩種不同的甲蟲。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A7","t":"物種形成"},{"w":"descent","pos":"n.","def":"coming from earlier family members or species","cn":"血統；由來","s":"The museum guide explained that whales are of land-animal ________, and the small bones in their bodies are clues to that past.","zh":"博物館導覽員解釋說鯨魚是陸地動物血統，而牠們體內的小骨頭就是那段過去的線索。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A8","t":"血統"},{"w":"vestigial","pos":"adj.","def":"still present in the body but no longer useful","cn":"退化的；殘留的","s":"Some snakes still have tiny ________ leg bones inside their bodies, although they have not used legs for millions of years.","zh":"有些蛇的體內仍有微小的退化的腿骨，雖然牠們已經數百萬年沒有使用腿了。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A9","t":"退化的"},{"w":"missing link","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a fossil that connects two groups of living things","cn":"缺失的環節","s":"Newspapers called the feathered dinosaur fossil a ______ ______, because it seemed to connect reptiles and modern birds.","zh":"報紙把這個有羽毛的恐龍化石稱為缺失的環節，因為它似乎連接了爬行動物和現代鳥類。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A10","t":"缺失的環節"},{"w":"tree of life","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a diagram showing how all living things are related","cn":"生命之樹","s":"The poster in the science lab shows a huge ______ ______ ______, and students can trace how fish, birds and humans are related.","zh":"科學實驗室裡的海報展示了一棵巨大的生命之樹，學生可以追溯魚類、鳥類和人類之間的關係。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A11","t":"生命之樹"},{"w":"coevolution","pos":"n.","def":"when two species change over time because of each other","cn":"共同演化","s":"Some flowers have long tubes and some moths have long tongues, and scientists see this as a clear example of ________.","zh":"有些花有長長的花管，而有些蛾有長長的口器，科學家把這視為共同演化的清楚例子。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A12","t":"共同演化"},{"w":"convergent evolution","pos":"n.phr.","def":"when unrelated animals develop similar features","cn":"趨同演化","s":"Sharks and dolphins are not closely related, but they both have smooth bodies and fins because of ______ ______.","zh":"鯊魚和海豚並不是近親，但因為趨同演化，牠們都有光滑的身體和鰭。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A13","t":"趨同演化"},{"w":"arms race","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a contest where each side keeps improving to beat the other","cn":"軍備競賽","s":"Cheetahs became faster to catch gazelles, while gazelles became faster to escape, so the two animals are locked in an ______ ______.","zh":"獵豹變得更快以捕捉瞪羚，而瞪羚也變得更快以逃脫，所以這兩種動物陷入了一場軍備競賽。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A14","t":"軍備競賽"},{"w":"selection pressure","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a force in nature that affects which animals survive","cn":"選擇壓力","s":"When the winters became colder, there was strong ______ ______ on the deer, and only those with thick coats survived.","zh":"當冬天變得更冷時，鹿群受到強大的選擇壓力，只有毛皮厚的鹿才存活下來。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A15","t":"選擇壓力"},{"w":"advantageous","pos":"adj.","def":"helpful and giving a better chance of success","cn":"有利的","s":"Long necks were ________ for giraffes because they could reach leaves high in the trees, so more long-necked giraffes survived.","zh":"長脖子對長頸鹿是有利的，因為牠們能吃到樹上高處的葉子，所以有更多長脖子的長頸鹿存活下來。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A16","t":"有利的"},{"w":"outcompete","pos":"v.","def":"to do better than others in getting food or space","cn":"競爭勝過","s":"Grey squirrels were brought to Britain from America, and they ________ the native red squirrels in many forests.","zh":"灰松鼠從美洲被帶到英國，而牠們在許多森林中競爭勝過了本地的紅松鼠。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A17","t":"競爭勝過"},{"w":"finch","pos":"n.","def":"a small bird with a short, strong beak","cn":"雀鳥","s":"Darwin studied the different ________ on the Galápagos Islands, and he noticed that their beaks matched the food on each island.","zh":"達爾文研究了加拉巴哥群島上不同的雀鳥，並注意到牠們的喙與每個島上的食物相符。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A18","t":"雀鳥"},{"w":"beak","pos":"n.","def":"the hard, pointed mouth of a bird","cn":"鳥喙","s":"Birds that crack hard seeds usually have a thick ________, but birds that catch insects often have a thin one.","zh":"會咬開堅硬種子的鳥通常有厚實的鳥喙，但捕捉昆蟲的鳥通常有細長的喙。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A19","t":"鳥喙"},{"w":"primordial","pos":"adj.","def":"existing at the very beginning of time","cn":"原始的；最初的","s":"Some scientists think life began in a ________ soup of chemicals in the ocean, but others believe it started near hot vents.","zh":"有些科學家認為生命起源於海洋中化學物質組成的原始的湯，但其他人相信生命始於熱泉噴口附近。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A20","t":"原始的"},{"w":"single-celled","pos":"adj.","def":"made of only one cell","cn":"單細胞的","s":"The first living things on Earth were tiny ________ creatures, and they existed alone for billions of years before animals appeared.","zh":"地球上最早的生物是微小的單細胞的生物，而牠們在動物出現之前獨自存在了數十億年。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A21","t":"單細胞的"},{"w":"multicellular","pos":"adj.","def":"made of many cells working together","cn":"多細胞的","s":"Plants and animals are ________ living things, but bacteria are made of just one cell each.","zh":"植物和動物都是多細胞的生物，但細菌每個都只由一個細胞組成。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A22","t":"多細胞的"},{"w":"microorganism","pos":"n.","def":"a living thing too small to see without a microscope","cn":"微生物","s":"A spoonful of garden soil contains millions of ________, and many of them help plants grow by breaking down dead leaves.","zh":"一湯匙的花園土壤含有數百萬個微生物，而且其中許多會分解枯葉來幫助植物生長。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A23","t":"微生物"},{"w":"naturalist","pos":"n.","def":"a person who studies plants and animals in nature","cn":"博物學家","s":"As a young ________, Darwin collected beetles and birds, and his notes later helped him form his famous theory.","zh":"年輕時身為博物學家的達爾文收集甲蟲和鳥類，而他的筆記後來幫助他形成了著名的理論。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A24","t":"博物學家"},{"w":"biologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies living things","cn":"生物學家","s":"My cousin works as a ________ in Taiwan, and she spends weeks in the mountains counting frogs and taking photos.","zh":"我的表姐在台灣擔任生物學家，她會花好幾週在山裡數青蛙和拍照。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A25","t":"生物學家"},{"w":"variant","pos":"n.","def":"a form of something that is slightly different","cn":"變種；變體","s":"Doctors watched the new ________ of the virus closely, because it spread faster than the earlier type.","zh":"醫生密切觀察這種病毒的新變種，因為它比較早的類型傳播得更快。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A26","t":"變種"},{"w":"ancestral","pos":"adj.","def":"belonging to earlier family members or species","cn":"祖先的","s":"Scientists studied the ________ home of the first dogs, and they found that wolves there lived close to early humans.","zh":"科學家研究了最早的狗的祖先的家園，並發現那裡的狼和早期人類生活得很近。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A27","t":"祖先的"},{"w":"taxonomy","pos":"n.","def":"the science of naming and grouping living things","cn":"分類學","s":"Students learn ________ in their first year, so they can name animals correctly and know which group each one belongs to.","zh":"學生在第一年學習分類學，好讓他們能正確地為動物命名並知道每種動物屬於哪一類。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A28","t":"分類學"},{"w":"peppered moth","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a moth that changed colour when cities became sooty","cn":"樺尺蛾","s":"During the Industrial Revolution, dark ______ ______ became more common, because they were hidden on dirty black trees.","zh":"在工業革命期間，深色的樺尺蛾變得更常見，因為牠們能隱藏在骯髒的黑色樹幹上。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A29","t":"樺尺蛾"},{"w":"superbug","pos":"n.","def":"a germ that common medicines can no longer kill","cn":"超級細菌","s":"Doctors warn that taking medicine you do not need can create a ________, and then ordinary drugs will stop working.","zh":"醫生警告服用不需要的藥物可能會產生超級細菌，然後一般的藥物就會失效。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A30","t":"超級細菌"},{"w":"drug-resistant","pos":"adj.","def":"not affected by medicines that once worked","cn":"抗藥性的","s":"The hospital found a ________ infection in one patient, so the nurses moved him to a separate room.","zh":"醫院在一名病人身上發現了抗藥性的感染，所以護理師把他移到單獨的病房。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A31","t":"抗藥性的"},{"w":"giraffe","pos":"n.","def":"a tall African animal with a very long neck","cn":"長頸鹿","s":"Male ________ swing their long necks at each other when they fight, and the stronger one usually wins a partner.","zh":"雄長頸鹿打鬥時會互相揮動長脖子，而較強壯的那一隻通常會贏得伴侶。","part":"A","sec":"Evolution & Natural Selection 演化與天擇","lab":"A32","t":"長頸鹿"},{"w":"hominid","pos":"n.","def":"a member of the group including humans and great apes","cn":"人科動物","s":"The team discovered the teeth of an early ________ in a cave, and they believe it lived about two million years ago.","zh":"研究團隊在一個洞穴中發現了一個早期人科動物的牙齒，他們相信牠生活在大約兩百萬年前。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A33","t":"人科動物"},{"w":"Homo sapiens","pos":"n.","def":"the scientific name for modern humans","cn":"智人","s":"______ ______ first appeared in Africa, and over thousands of years our species spread to every continent.","zh":"智人最早出現在非洲，而經過數千年，我們這個物種擴散到了每一個大陸。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A34","t":"智人"},{"w":"Neanderthal","pos":"n.","def":"an early human who lived in Europe and Asia","cn":"尼安德塔人","s":"Many people today carry a little ________ DNA, because our ancestors met and had children with them long ago.","zh":"現今許多人身上帶有一點尼安德塔人的DNA，因為我們的祖先很久以前曾與他們相遇並生下孩子。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A35","t":"尼安德塔人"},{"w":"great ape","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a large primate such as a gorilla or chimpanzee","cn":"大型猿類","s":"The zoo built a large forest area for every ______ ______, because these clever animals need space to climb and explore.","zh":"動物園為每一隻大型猿類建造了大片森林區，因為這些聰明的動物需要空間攀爬和探索。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A36","t":"大型猿類"},{"w":"chimpanzee","pos":"n.","def":"an African ape that is closely related to humans","cn":"黑猩猩","s":"Jane Goodall watched a ________ use a stick to catch termites, and this showed that animals can make tools too.","zh":"珍古德看見一隻黑猩猩用樹枝捕捉白蟻，而這顯示動物也會製作工具。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A37","t":"黑猩猩"},{"w":"gorilla","pos":"n.","def":"the largest ape, living in African forests","cn":"大猩猩","s":"The silverback ________ looked scary, but he was very gentle with the babies in his family.","zh":"那隻銀背大猩猩看起來很可怕，但他對家族裡的寶寶非常溫柔。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A38","t":"大猩猩"},{"w":"orangutan","pos":"n.","def":"a red-haired ape from Borneo and Sumatra","cn":"紅毛猩猩","s":"The young ________ stays with its mother for about eight years, and she teaches it which fruits are safe to eat.","zh":"年幼的紅毛猩猩會和媽媽待在一起大約八年，而媽媽會教牠哪些水果可以安全食用。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A39","t":"紅毛猩猩"},{"w":"bonobo","pos":"n.","def":"a peaceful ape closely related to the chimpanzee","cn":"巴諾布猿","s":"A ________ group usually solves fights by sharing food and hugging, so scientists call them the peaceful apes.","zh":"巴諾布猿群體通常以分享食物和擁抱來解決爭吵，所以科學家稱牠們為和平的猿類。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A40","t":"巴諾布猿"},{"w":"bipedal","pos":"adj.","def":"walking on two legs","cn":"雙足行走的","s":"Our early ancestors became ________ on the open grasslands, and walking upright left their hands free to carry food.","zh":"我們早期的祖先在開闊的草原上變成雙足行走的，而直立行走讓他們的雙手能空出來搬運食物。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A41","t":"雙足行走的"},{"w":"upright","pos":"adj.","def":"standing straight up","cn":"直立的","s":"Bears can stand ________ for a short time, but they usually walk on four legs when they look for food.","zh":"熊可以短時間直立站著，但牠們找食物時通常用四條腿走路。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A42","t":"直立"},{"w":"posture","pos":"n.","def":"the way you hold your body","cn":"姿勢","s":"Sitting at a desk for hours is bad for your ________, and doctors say our spines evolved for walking, not sitting.","zh":"在書桌前坐好幾個小時對你的姿勢不好，醫生說我們的脊椎是為了走路而演化的，而不是為了坐著。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A43","t":"姿勢"},{"w":"opposable thumb","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a thumb that can touch the other fingers","cn":"可對握的拇指","s":"We can hold a pencil and open a jar easily, because we have an ______ ______ that works with our other fingers.","zh":"我們能輕鬆握筆和打開罐子，因為我們有一根能與其他手指配合的可對握的拇指。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A44","t":"可對握的拇指"},{"w":"toolmaking","pos":"n.","def":"the activity of making tools","cn":"工具製作","s":"Early ________ began with simple sharp stones, but over time people learned to make spears, needles and fishing hooks.","zh":"早期的工具製作從簡單的尖銳石頭開始，但隨著時間推移，人們學會了製作矛、針和魚鉤。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A45","t":"工具製作"},{"w":"early humans","pos":"n.phr.","def":"people who lived very long ago","cn":"早期人類","s":"______ ______ learned to control fire, and cooking their food gave them more energy for their growing brains.","zh":"早期人類學會了控制火，而烹煮食物讓他們有更多能量供應逐漸變大的大腦。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A46","t":"早期人類"},{"w":"interbreed / interbred / interbred","pos":"v.","def":"to produce young with a different group or species","cn":"雜交繁殖","s":"Modern humans and Neanderthals ________ in the past, so traces of their DNA still exist in many people today.","zh":"現代人類和尼安德塔人過去曾雜交繁殖，所以他們DNA的痕跡至今仍存在於許多人身上。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A47","t":"雜交繁殖"},{"w":"skeletal","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to the bones of a body","cn":"骨骼的","s":"The doctor studied the ________ remains carefully, and she found that the person had walked long distances every day.","zh":"這位醫生仔細研究了這些骨骼的遺骸，並發現這個人生前每天都走很長的路。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A48","t":"骨骼的"},{"w":"jawbone","pos":"n.","def":"the bone that holds the lower teeth","cn":"顎骨","s":"The ancient ________ was small and had worn teeth, so scientists guessed the person ate tough plants.","zh":"這塊古老的顎骨很小，牙齒也磨損了，所以科學家推測這個人吃的是堅韌的植物。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A49","t":"顎骨"},{"w":"spine","pos":"n.","def":"the row of bones down the middle of your back","cn":"脊椎","s":"Our ________ has an S-shape that helps us walk on two legs, but it also explains why so many adults get back pain.","zh":"我們的脊椎呈S形，幫助我們用雙腿走路，但這也解釋了為什麼這麼多成年人會背痛。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A50","t":"脊椎"},{"w":"primatologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies monkeys and apes","cn":"靈長類動物學家","s":"The ________ lived in the rainforest for two years, and she learned to recognise every monkey by its face.","zh":"那位靈長類動物學家在雨林裡住了兩年，而她學會了從臉認出每一隻猴子。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A51","t":"靈長類動物學家"},{"w":"anthropologist","pos":"n.","def":"a person who studies human societies and cultures","cn":"人類學家","s":"An ________ visited the mountain village to study its traditions, and the villagers taught her their old songs.","zh":"一位人類學家到山村研究當地的傳統，而村民教她唱他們古老的歌謠。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A52","t":"人類學家"},{"w":"anthropology","pos":"n.","def":"the study of humans, their history and culture","cn":"人類學","s":"My sister is studying ________ at university, because she wants to understand how people lived thousands of years ago.","zh":"我姐姐在大學主修人類學，因為她想了解人們數千年前是如何生活的。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A53","t":"人類學"},{"w":"body hair","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the hair that grows on the body","cn":"體毛","s":"Humans lost most of their ______ ______ over time, and some scientists think this helped them stay cool while running.","zh":"人類隨著時間失去了大部分的體毛，而有些科學家認為這幫助他們在奔跑時保持涼爽。","part":"A","sec":"Human Evolution & Our Relatives 人類演化與近親","lab":"A54","t":"體毛"},{"w":"cell","pos":"n.","def":"the smallest living unit of a plant or animal","cn":"細胞","s":"Every ________ in your body contains instructions, and these instructions tell it whether to become skin, bone or blood.","zh":"你身體裡的每一個細胞都含有指令，而這些指令告訴它要變成皮膚、骨頭還是血液。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A55","t":"細胞"},{"w":"nucleus","pos":"n.","def":"the centre of a cell that holds the DNA","cn":"細胞核","s":"We looked at onion cells under the microscope, and we could see a dark ________ in the middle of each one.","zh":"我們在顯微鏡下觀察洋蔥細胞，並能看見每個細胞中間都有一個深色的細胞核。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A56","t":"細胞核"},{"w":"chromosome","pos":"n.","def":"a thread-like structure in a cell that carries genes","cn":"染色體","s":"Humans normally have 46 ________ in each cell, and we receive half from our mother and half from our father.","zh":"人類每個細胞通常有46條染色體，我們一半來自母親，一半來自父親。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A57","t":"染色體"},{"w":"gene","pos":"n.","def":"a part of DNA that controls a feature like eye colour","cn":"基因","s":"Scientists found a ________ that affects how tall people grow, but food and sleep also play an important role.","zh":"科學家發現了一個會影響人們長多高的基因，但食物和睡眠也扮演重要的角色。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A58","t":"基因"},{"w":"double helix","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the twisted ladder shape of DNA","cn":"雙螺旋","s":"Our class built a model of DNA with sweets and sticks, and it twisted into a ______ ______ just like the real thing.","zh":"我們班用糖果和小棍子做了一個DNA模型，而它扭成了一個像真的一樣的雙螺旋。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A59","t":"雙螺旋"},{"w":"base pair","pos":"n.phr.","def":"two matching chemical units that form a step in DNA","cn":"鹼基對","s":"Human DNA has about three billion ______ ______, so reading the whole code took scientists many years.","zh":"人類DNA大約有三十億個鹼基對，所以科學家花了許多年才讀完整個密碼。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A60","t":"鹼基對"},{"w":"molecule","pos":"n.","def":"the smallest unit of a substance made of atoms","cn":"分子","s":"DNA is a very long ________, but it is folded so tightly that it fits inside a tiny cell.","zh":"DNA是一個非常長的分子，但它摺疊得非常緊密，所以能放進微小的細胞裡。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A61","t":"分子"},{"w":"enzyme","pos":"n.","def":"a substance in the body that speeds up chemical changes","cn":"酵素","s":"Our saliva contains an ________ that starts breaking down rice, so bread tastes sweeter if you chew it for a long time.","zh":"我們的唾液含有一種會開始分解米飯的酵素，所以麵包嚼久了吃起來會比較甜。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A62","t":"酵素"},{"w":"cell division","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the process in which one cell splits into two","cn":"細胞分裂","s":"A cut on your finger heals quickly, because ______ ______ makes new skin cells to fill the gap.","zh":"你手指上的傷口很快就會癒合，因為細胞分裂會產生新的皮膚細胞來填補缺口。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A63","t":"細胞分裂"},{"w":"membrane","pos":"n.","def":"a thin layer that covers a cell","cn":"薄膜","s":"The cell ________ works like a gate, and it decides which substances can enter or leave the cell.","zh":"細胞薄膜就像一扇門，而它決定哪些物質可以進出細胞。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A64","t":"薄膜"},{"w":"mitochondria","pos":"n.","def":"parts of a cell that make energy","cn":"粒線體","s":"Muscle cells contain many ________, because they need a lot of energy when we run or lift things.","zh":"肌肉細胞含有許多粒線體，因為我們跑步或舉東西時它們需要大量能量。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A65","t":"粒線體"},{"w":"RNA","pos":"n.","def":"a molecule that helps turn DNA instructions into proteins","cn":"核糖核酸","s":"Some vaccines use ________ to teach the body how to fight a virus, and this new method was developed very quickly.","zh":"有些疫苗利用核糖核酸教導身體如何對抗病毒，而這種新方法發展得非常快。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A66","t":"核糖核酸"},{"w":"sequencing","pos":"n.","def":"finding the exact order of units in DNA","cn":"定序","s":"DNA ________ used to cost millions of dollars, but now a person's whole genome can be read for a few hundred.","zh":"DNA定序過去要花數百萬美元，但現在一個人的全基因組只要幾百美元就能讀取。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A67","t":"定序"},{"w":"amino acid","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a small unit that joins with others to build proteins","cn":"胺基酸","s":"Meat, beans and eggs give us every ______ ______ we need, so vegetarians must choose their food carefully.","zh":"肉類、豆類和蛋提供我們所需的每一種胺基酸，所以素食者必須小心選擇食物。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A68","t":"胺基酸"},{"w":"egg cell","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the female cell that can grow into a baby","cn":"卵細胞","s":"An ______ ______ is one of the largest cells in the human body, and you can almost see it without a microscope.","zh":"卵細胞是人體中最大的細胞之一，而你幾乎不用顯微鏡就能看見它。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A69","t":"卵細胞"},{"w":"fertilisation","pos":"n.","def":"when male and female cells join to start new life","cn":"受精","s":"Frogs lay their eggs in the water of ponds, and ________ happens outside the mother's body there.","zh":"青蛙把卵產在池塘的水中，而受精就在那裡、在母體之外發生。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A70","t":"受精"},{"w":"embryo","pos":"n.","def":"an animal or human in the very early stage of growth","cn":"胚胎","s":"The chicken ________ grows inside the egg for about three weeks, and then the chick breaks the shell.","zh":"雞的胚胎在蛋裡生長大約三週，然後小雞就會啄破蛋殼。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A71","t":"胚胎"},{"w":"stem cell","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a basic cell that can become many types of cell","cn":"幹細胞","s":"Doctors hope that ______ ______ can repair damaged hearts, but more research is needed before this treatment is safe.","zh":"醫生希望幹細胞能修復受損的心臟，但在這種治療安全之前還需要更多研究。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A72","t":"幹細胞"},{"w":"tissue","pos":"n.","def":"a group of similar cells that work together","cn":"組織","s":"The scientist took a small piece of ________ from the leaf, and she studied the cells under a microscope.","zh":"科學家從葉子上取下一小片組織，並在顯微鏡下研究那些細胞。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A73","t":"組織"},{"w":"organ","pos":"n.","def":"a body part such as the heart that does a special job","cn":"器官","s":"The skin is actually the largest ________ of the human body, and it protects us from germs and heat.","zh":"皮膚其實是人體最大的器官，而它保護我們免受細菌和高溫的傷害。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A74","t":"器官"},{"w":"microbe","pos":"n.","def":"a tiny living thing such as a bacterium","cn":"微生物；細菌","s":"Yoghurt contains many friendly ________, and they help our stomachs digest the food we eat more easily.","zh":"優格含有許多有益的微生物，而它們幫助我們的胃更容易消化我們吃下的食物。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A75","t":"微生物"},{"w":"biochemistry","pos":"n.","def":"the study of chemical processes in living things","cn":"生物化學","s":"She enjoyed both biology and chemistry at school, so she decided to study ________ at university.","zh":"她在學校時喜歡生物和化學兩科，所以她決定在大學主修生物化學。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A76","t":"生物化學"},{"w":"geneticist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies genes","cn":"遺傳學家","s":"The ________ explained the results to the family, and she said the baby's condition was not passed down from the parents.","zh":"遺傳學家向這家人解釋了結果，並說寶寶的狀況並不是從父母遺傳下來的。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A77","t":"遺傳學家"},{"w":"genetics","pos":"n.","def":"the science of how features pass from parents to children","cn":"遺傳學","s":"We studied ________ this term, and now I understand why I have curly hair like my grandfather.","zh":"我們這學期學了遺傳學，現在我明白為什麼我會像祖父一樣有一頭捲髮。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A78","t":"遺傳學"},{"w":"petri dish","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a small round dish used to grow germs in a lab","cn":"培養皿","s":"We put a little bread in a ______ ______, and after a week a green mould had covered it.","zh":"我們在培養皿裡放了一點麵包，而一週後綠色的黴菌已經把它覆蓋了。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A79","t":"培養皿"},{"w":"saliva","pos":"n.","def":"the liquid in your mouth","cn":"唾液","s":"The test only needs a little ________, so you just spit into a small tube and send it to the lab.","zh":"這項檢測只需要一點點唾液，所以你只要吐進一根小管子裡然後寄到實驗室。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A80","t":"唾液"},{"w":"cheek swab","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a cotton stick rubbed inside the mouth to collect cells","cn":"口腔拭子","s":"The police took a ______ ______ from each worker, because they wanted to compare their DNA with the evidence.","zh":"警方從每位員工身上採集了口腔拭子，因為他們想把他們的DNA和證據作比對。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A81","t":"口腔拭子"},{"w":"decode","pos":"v.","def":"to find the meaning of a code","cn":"解碼；破譯","s":"Scientists worked for thirteen years to ________ the human genome, and they finally finished the project in 2003.","zh":"科學家努力了十三年來解碼人類基因組，並終於在2003年完成這項計畫。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A82","t":"解碼"},{"w":"twin","pos":"n.","def":"one of two children born at the same time to the same mother","cn":"雙胞胎","s":"My friend is a ________, and even our teachers cannot tell her and her sister apart.","zh":"我的朋友是雙胞胎之一，連我們的老師都分不出她和她的姐妹。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A83","t":"雙胞胎"},{"w":"cellular","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to cells","cn":"細胞的","s":"Smoking causes damage at a ________ level, so the harm starts long before a person notices any illness.","zh":"吸菸會在細胞的層面造成傷害，所以傷害早在一個人察覺任何疾病之前就開始了。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A84","t":"細胞的"},{"w":"fruit fly","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a tiny fly often used in genetics experiments","cn":"果蠅","s":"Scientists often study the ______ ______, because it breeds very quickly and shares many genes with humans.","zh":"科學家常常研究果蠅，因為牠繁殖得非常快，而且和人類有許多共同的基因。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A85","t":"果蠅"},{"w":"lab rat","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a rat used for scientific experiments","cn":"實驗鼠","s":"The new medicine was first tested on a ______ ______, but it must also be tested on human volunteers before it is sold.","zh":"這種新藥先在實驗鼠身上做了測試，但在販售之前也必須在人類志願者身上測試。","part":"A","sec":"Cells, DNA & Genes 細胞、DNA與基因","lab":"A86","t":"實驗鼠"},{"w":"inheritance","pos":"n.","def":"features passed from parents to children","cn":"遺傳","s":"Curly hair in our family is a clear case of ________, because my mother, my grandmother and I all have it.","zh":"我們家的捲髮是遺傳的明顯例子，因為我媽媽、我外婆和我都有捲髮。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A87","t":"遺傳"},{"w":"mutation","pos":"n.","def":"a change in a gene","cn":"突變","s":"A small ________ in one gene gave the cat six toes on each paw, and her kittens had extra toes too.","zh":"一個基因的小突變讓這隻貓每隻腳掌都有六根趾頭，而牠的小貓也有多出來的趾頭。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A88","t":"突變"},{"w":"mutate","pos":"v.","def":"to change in form because of a gene change","cn":"突變","s":"Flu viruses ________ quickly every single year, so many people need a new vaccine each autumn.","zh":"流感病毒每一年都快速突變，所以許多人每年秋天都需要接種新疫苗。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A89","t":"突變"},{"w":"recessive","pos":"adj.","def":"only shown when a child gets the same gene from both parents","cn":"隱性的","s":"Blue eyes are caused by a ________ gene, so two brown-eyed parents can still have a blue-eyed baby.","zh":"藍眼睛是由隱性的基因造成的，所以兩個棕眼睛的父母仍然可能生下藍眼睛的寶寶。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A90","t":"隱性的"},{"w":"genotype","pos":"n.","def":"the set of genes a living thing has","cn":"基因型","s":"Two plants may look the same, but they can have a different ________, so their seeds may grow differently.","zh":"兩株植物可能看起來一樣，但它們可能有不同的基因型，所以它們的種子可能長得不一樣。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A91","t":"基因型"},{"w":"phenotype","pos":"n.","def":"the features you can see, such as size or colour","cn":"表現型","s":"A person's ________ includes height and hair colour, and it depends on both genes and lifestyle.","zh":"一個人的表現型包括身高和髮色，而它取決於基因和生活方式兩者。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A92","t":"表現型"},{"w":"carrier","pos":"n.","def":"a person who has a gene but does not show its effect","cn":"帶原者；攜帶者","s":"My uncle is a ________ of the gene, but he is healthy, so the doctor told him to tell his children.","zh":"我舅舅是這個基因的攜帶者，但他很健康，所以醫生要他告訴他的孩子們。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A93","t":"攜帶者"},{"w":"gene pool","pos":"n.phr.","def":"all the genes in a group of animals or people","cn":"基因庫","s":"The small island population has a limited ______ ______, so the zoo brought in new animals from other places.","zh":"這個小島族群的基因庫很有限，所以動物園從其他地方引進了新的動物。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A94","t":"基因庫"},{"w":"inbreeding","pos":"n.","def":"breeding between closely related animals","cn":"近親繁殖","s":"Many purebred dogs suffer from health problems, because years of ________ have made their genes too similar.","zh":"許多純種狗受健康問題所苦，因為多年的近親繁殖讓牠們的基因太過相似。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A95","t":"近親繁殖"},{"w":"eye colour","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the colour of the coloured part of the eye","cn":"眼睛顏色","s":"Most babies in Taiwan are born with dark eyes, but ______ ______ can change during the first year in some children.","zh":"台灣大多數嬰兒出生時是深色眼睛，但有些孩子的眼睛顏色在第一年內可能會改變。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A96","t":"眼睛顏色"},{"w":"freckle","pos":"n.","def":"a small brown spot on the skin","cn":"雀斑","s":"She has many ________ on her nose like her father, and they get darker when she spends time in the sun.","zh":"她的鼻子上有很多雀斑，跟她爸爸一樣，而且她曬太陽時雀斑會變得更深。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A97","t":"雀斑"},{"w":"dimple","pos":"n.","def":"a small hollow in the cheek when you smile","cn":"酒窩","s":"Everyone in the family has a ________ in the left cheek, so people can easily guess that we are related.","zh":"家裡每個人的左臉頰都有一個酒窩，所以人們很容易猜到我們是一家人。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A98","t":"酒窩"},{"w":"left-handed","pos":"adj.","def":"using the left hand more easily than the right","cn":"左撇子的","s":"Both of my parents are ________, so it was not surprising that I also write with my left hand.","zh":"我的父母都是左撇子的，所以我也用左手寫字並不令人意外。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A99","t":"左撇子的"},{"w":"birth defect","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a health problem that a baby is born with","cn":"先天缺陷","s":"Doctors advise pregnant women to take certain vitamins, because they lower the risk of a ______ ______.","zh":"醫生建議孕婦服用某些維生素，因為它們能降低先天缺陷的風險。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A100","t":"先天缺陷"},{"w":"congenital","pos":"adj.","def":"present from birth","cn":"先天的","s":"The puppy had a ________ heart problem, but the vet performed an operation and it now runs around happily.","zh":"那隻小狗有先天的心臟問題，但獸醫為牠動了手術，現在牠開心地到處跑。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A101","t":"先天的"},{"w":"blood type","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the group your blood belongs to, such as A or O","cn":"血型","s":"Your ______ ______ is passed down from your parents, so a family's types can help doctors find a match.","zh":"你的血型是從父母遺傳下來的，所以一個家庭的血型可以幫助醫生找到配對。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A102","t":"血型"},{"w":"pedigree","pos":"n.","def":"the recorded family history of an animal","cn":"血統證明；系譜","s":"The breeder showed us the puppy's ________, and it listed the dog's parents and grandparents.","zh":"繁殖者給我們看了小狗的血統證明，而上面列出了這隻狗的父母和祖父母。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A103","t":"血統證明"},{"w":"purebred","pos":"adj.","def":"having parents of the same breed","cn":"純種的","s":"A ________ cat can be very expensive, but shelter cats are often healthier and cost much less.","zh":"一隻純種的貓可能非常昂貴，但收容所的貓往往更健康，花費也少得多。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A104","t":"純種的"},{"w":"crossbreed / crossbred / crossbred","pos":"v.","def":"to mix two breeds to make a new type","cn":"雜交育種","s":"Farmers ________ two kinds of rice, and the new type grows well in dry weather.","zh":"農民把兩種稻米雜交育種，而新品種在乾燥的天氣中長得很好。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A105","t":"雜交育種"},{"w":"upbringing","pos":"n.","def":"the way a child is cared for and taught at home","cn":"教養；成長環境","s":"Twins who grow up apart can be very similar, but their ________ still shapes their habits and interests.","zh":"分開長大的雙胞胎可能非常相似，但他們的成長環境仍會塑造他們的習慣和興趣。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A106","t":"成長環境"},{"w":"epigenetics","pos":"n.","def":"the study of how lifestyle can switch genes on or off","cn":"表觀遺傳學","s":"________ shows that stress and diet can affect how our genes work, although the DNA itself does not change.","zh":"表觀遺傳學顯示壓力和飲食會影響我們的基因如何運作，雖然DNA本身並沒有改變。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A107","t":"表觀遺傳學"},{"w":"fraternal","pos":"adj.","def":"(of twins) from two different eggs","cn":"異卵的","s":"My brother and I are ________ twins, so we look quite different and we were born ten minutes apart.","zh":"我哥哥和我是異卵的雙胞胎，所以我們長得很不一樣，而且出生時間相差十分鐘。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A108","t":"異卵的"},{"w":"sibling","pos":"n.","def":"a brother or sister","cn":"兄弟姊妹","s":"Each ________ in my family has a different hobby, although we all grew up in the same small apartment.","zh":"我家的每個兄弟姊妹都有不同的嗜好，雖然我們都在同一間小公寓長大。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A109","t":"兄弟姊妹"},{"w":"biological parent","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the parent who gave you your genes","cn":"親生父母","s":"Adopted children sometimes want to find their ______ ______, because they are curious about their family history.","zh":"被收養的孩子有時想找到他們的親生父母，因為他們對自己的家族史感到好奇。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A110","t":"親生父母"},{"w":"gene expression","pos":"n.phr.","def":"how strongly a gene is turned on in a cell","cn":"基因表現","s":"Exercise can change ______ ______ in muscle cells, so regular training helps the body build stronger muscles.","zh":"運動可以改變肌肉細胞中的基因表現，所以規律訓練能幫助身體練出更強壯的肌肉。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A111","t":"基因表現"},{"w":"heritable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be passed from parent to child","cn":"可遺傳的","s":"Height is highly ________, but children today are taller than their grandparents because they eat better food.","zh":"身高是高度可遺傳的，但今天的孩子比他們的祖父母高，因為他們吃得更好。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A112","t":"可遺傳的"},{"w":"birthmark","pos":"n.","def":"a coloured mark on the skin from birth","cn":"胎記","s":"The baby has a small red ________ on her arm, but the doctor said it will fade as she grows.","zh":"寶寶的手臂上有一個小小的紅色胎記，但醫生說它會隨著她長大而變淡。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A113","t":"胎記"},{"w":"colour blindness","pos":"n.phr.","def":"being unable to see some colours clearly","cn":"色盲","s":"______ ______ is much more common in boys, because the gene for it is carried on the X chromosome.","zh":"色盲在男孩中常見得多，因為與它相關的基因位於X染色體上。","part":"A","sec":"Inheritance & Genetic Variation 遺傳與基因變異","lab":"A114","t":"色盲"},{"w":"CRISPR","pos":"n.","def":"a tool that lets scientists cut and change DNA","cn":"基因剪刀CRISPR","s":"Scientists used ________ to remove a disease gene from mice, and the treated mice stayed healthy.","zh":"科學家使用基因剪刀CRISPR從老鼠身上移除一個致病基因，而接受治療的老鼠保持健康。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A115","t":"基因剪刀CRISPR"},{"w":"gene therapy","pos":"n.phr.","def":"treating illness by changing a patient's genes","cn":"基因療法","s":"The boy could not see well since birth, but ______ ______ improved his sight, and now he can read books.","zh":"這個男孩從出生起視力就不好，但基因療法改善了他的視力，現在他可以讀書了。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A116","t":"基因療法"},{"w":"paternity test","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a DNA test to find out who a child's father is","cn":"親子鑑定","s":"The court asked for a ______ ______, because the man said he was not the child's father.","zh":"法院要求進行親子鑑定，因為那名男子說他不是孩子的父親。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A117","t":"親子鑑定"},{"w":"forensic","pos":"adj.","def":"using science to help solve crimes","cn":"鑑識的","s":"The ________ team found a single hair at the scene, and its DNA led them to the thief.","zh":"鑑識的小組在現場發現了一根頭髮，而它的DNA帶領他們找到了小偷。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A118","t":"鑑識的"},{"w":"transgenic","pos":"adj.","def":"having genes added from another species","cn":"基因轉殖的","s":"The lab created ________ goats that produce a useful medicine in their milk, so patients can get it more cheaply.","zh":"實驗室培育出基因轉殖的山羊，牠們的奶中含有一種有用的藥物，所以病人能更便宜地取得。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A119","t":"基因轉殖的"},{"w":"designer baby","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a baby whose genes are chosen or changed by parents","cn":"訂製嬰兒","s":"Many people worry about the idea of a ______ ______, because rich parents might choose intelligence or good looks for their children.","zh":"許多人擔心訂製嬰兒的想法，因為有錢的父母可能會為孩子挑選聰明才智或好看的外表。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A120","t":"訂製嬰兒"},{"w":"bioethics","pos":"n.","def":"the study of right and wrong in medicine and biology","cn":"生命倫理學","s":"Our class debated gene editing in a ________ lesson, and most students felt it should only be used to cure disease.","zh":"我們班在一堂生命倫理學課上辯論基因編輯，而大多數學生認為它只應該被用來治療疾病。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A121","t":"生命倫理學"},{"w":"precision medicine","pos":"n.phr.","def":"treatment planned for a person's own genes","cn":"精準醫療","s":"______ ______ lets doctors choose the right cancer drug for each patient, so the treatment works better and causes fewer problems.","zh":"精準醫療讓醫生能為每位病人選擇合適的抗癌藥物，所以治療效果更好，產生的問題也更少。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A122","t":"精準醫療"},{"w":"insulin","pos":"n.","def":"a hormone that controls sugar in the blood","cn":"胰島素","s":"Today, bacteria are used to make human ________, so it is much cheaper than it was fifty years ago.","zh":"今天人們利用細菌來製造人類胰島素，所以它比五十年前便宜得多。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A123","t":"胰島素"},{"w":"pharmaceutical","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to making and selling medicines","cn":"製藥的","s":"A large ________ company paid for the research, but the scientists promised to share their results with everyone.","zh":"一家大型製藥的公司資助了這項研究，但科學家承諾會與所有人分享他們的研究結果。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A124","t":"製藥的"},{"w":"clinical trial","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a test of a new treatment on volunteers","cn":"臨床試驗","s":"My aunt joined a ______ ______ for a new medicine, and the nurses checked her health every week.","zh":"我阿姨參加了一項新藥的臨床試驗，而護理師每週都檢查她的健康狀況。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A125","t":"臨床試驗"},{"w":"test tube","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a thin glass tube used in science labs","cn":"試管","s":"The student carefully poured the blue liquid into a ______ ______, and then she added two drops of acid.","zh":"那位學生小心地把藍色液體倒進試管，然後她加了兩滴酸液。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A126","t":"試管"},{"w":"IVF","pos":"n.","def":"a method of joining egg and sperm outside the body","cn":"試管嬰兒療程","s":"The couple tried for years to have a baby, so they finally chose ________, and their daughter was born last spring.","zh":"這對夫妻多年來一直想要孩子，所以他們最後選擇了試管嬰兒療程，而他們的女兒在去年春天出生。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A127","t":"試管嬰兒療程"},{"w":"donor","pos":"n.","def":"a person who gives blood or body parts to help others","cn":"捐贈者","s":"My father is a blood ________, and he visits the blood centre every few months to help patients.","zh":"我爸爸是一位捐血者，而他每隔幾個月就會去捐血中心幫助病人。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A128","t":"捐血者"},{"w":"bone marrow","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the soft tissue inside bones that makes blood","cn":"骨髓","s":"The girl needed new ______ ______, and luckily a stranger with a matching type agreed to help her.","zh":"那個女孩需要新的骨髓，幸運的是一位配型相符的陌生人同意幫助她。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A129","t":"骨髓"},{"w":"biobank","pos":"n.","def":"a store of blood and DNA samples for research","cn":"生物資料庫","s":"Thousands of volunteers gave samples to the national ________, so scientists can study which genes are linked to illness.","zh":"數千名志願者把樣本提供給國家生物資料庫，好讓科學家研究哪些基因和疾病有關。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A130","t":"生物資料庫"},{"w":"de-extinction","pos":"n.","def":"bringing an extinct animal back to life","cn":"復活滅絕物種","s":"Some companies are working on ________, but critics say we should protect living animals first.","zh":"有些公司正在研究復活滅絕物種，但批評者說我們應該先保護現存的動物。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A131","t":"復活滅絕物種"},{"w":"gene drive","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a method to spread a gene quickly through a population","cn":"基因驅動","s":"Scientists hope a ______ ______ could stop mosquitoes from carrying malaria, but releasing them into the wild is risky.","zh":"科學家希望基因驅動能阻止蚊子傳播瘧疾，但把牠們釋放到野外是有風險的。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A132","t":"基因驅動"},{"w":"pest-resistant","pos":"adj.","def":"not easily damaged by insects","cn":"抗蟲害的","s":"The farmer planted a ________ type of corn, so he did not need to spray as many chemicals.","zh":"那位農夫種了一種抗蟲害的玉米，所以他不需要噴灑那麼多化學藥劑。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A133","t":"抗蟲害的"},{"w":"golden rice","pos":"n.phr.","def":"rice changed to contain more vitamin A","cn":"黃金米","s":"______ ______ was created to help poor children get vitamin A, but some groups still oppose it.","zh":"黃金米是為了幫助貧窮兒童獲得維生素A而研發的，但有些團體仍然反對它。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A134","t":"黃金米"},{"w":"fluorescent","pos":"adj.","def":"giving off bright light under special lamps","cn":"螢光的","s":"Scientists added a jellyfish gene to the fish, and now they look ________ green under blue light.","zh":"科學家把一個水母基因加進魚的體內，而現在牠們在藍光下看起來是螢光的綠色。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A135","t":"螢光的"},{"w":"glow-in-the-dark","pos":"adj.","def":"shining in darkness","cn":"夜光的","s":"My little brother loves his ________ stickers, and he puts them on his ceiling so he can see stars at night.","zh":"我弟弟很喜歡他的夜光的貼紙，而他把它們貼在天花板上，這樣晚上就能看到星星。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A136","t":"夜光的"},{"w":"treatment","pos":"n.","def":"medical care for an illness or injury","cn":"治療","s":"The new ________ is expensive, but the government will pay for it because it can save many lives.","zh":"這種新治療很昂貴，但政府會支付費用，因為它能拯救許多生命。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A137","t":"治療"},{"w":"spit / spat / spat","pos":"v.","def":"to force liquid out of your mouth","cn":"吐（口水）","s":"For the ancestry kit, I ________ into a small tube, and a month later I got a report about my family's roots.","zh":"為了做祖源檢測組，我吐口水到一根小管子裡，一個月後我收到了一份關於我家族根源的報告。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A138","t":"吐"},{"w":"kit","pos":"n.","def":"a set of things packed together for a task","cn":"套組；工具包","s":"You can buy a DNA testing ________ online, but experts say the health results are not always accurate.","zh":"你可以在網路上買到DNA檢測套組，但專家說健康方面的結果不一定準確。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A139","t":"套組"},{"w":"biomedical","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to biology and medicine","cn":"生物醫學的","s":"Taiwan has invested heavily in ________ research, and many young scientists now work on new cancer treatments.","zh":"台灣大量投資於生物醫學的研究，現在許多年輕科學家致力於新的癌症治療。","part":"A","sec":"Genetic Technology & Medicine 基因科技與醫學","lab":"A140","t":"生物醫學的"},{"w":"ethology","pos":"n.","def":"the scientific study of animal behaviour","cn":"動物行為學","s":"She became interested in ________ after watching birds in the park, and she now studies how crows solve puzzles.","zh":"她在公園裡觀察鳥類之後對動物行為學產生了興趣，現在她研究烏鴉如何解決難題。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A141","t":"動物行為學"},{"w":"ethologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies animal behaviour","cn":"動物行為學家","s":"The ________ watched the wolves from a hidden hut, because she did not want her presence to change their behaviour.","zh":"那位動物行為學家從一間隱蔽的小屋觀察狼群，因為她不希望自己的存在改變牠們的行為。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A142","t":"動物行為學家"},{"w":"learned behaviour","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an action an animal learns rather than is born with","cn":"學習行為","s":"Opening milk bottles was a ______ ______ among some birds in Britain, and young birds copied it from older ones.","zh":"在英國，打開牛奶瓶是某些鳥類的學習行為，而年輕的鳥從年長的鳥那裡模仿學會了。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A143","t":"學習行為"},{"w":"imprinting","pos":"n.","def":"a young animal's quick bond with the first thing it sees","cn":"銘印","s":"Because of ________, the baby geese followed the scientist everywhere, and they treated him like their mother.","zh":"由於銘印，小鵝到處跟著那位科學家，而且牠們把他當作媽媽。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A144","t":"銘印"},{"w":"conditioning","pos":"n.","def":"training by linking an action with a reward or result","cn":"制約","s":"My dog runs to the kitchen when she hears the fridge open, and this is a simple example of ________.","zh":"我的狗一聽到冰箱打開就跑到廚房，而這是制約的一個簡單例子。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A145","t":"制約"},{"w":"reflex","pos":"n.","def":"an automatic movement you do not think about","cn":"反射動作","s":"When the ball flew towards his face, he closed his eyes as a ________, and he did not even think about it.","zh":"當球朝他的臉飛來時，他閉上眼睛作為反射動作，而他甚至沒有思考。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A146","t":"反射動作"},{"w":"birdsong","pos":"n.","def":"the musical sounds that birds make","cn":"鳥鳴","s":"I wake up to ________ every morning in spring, because the birds sing loudly to attract partners.","zh":"春天每天早上我都在鳥鳴聲中醒來，因為鳥兒大聲歌唱來吸引伴侶。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A147","t":"鳥鳴"},{"w":"chirp","pos":"v.","def":"(of a bird or insect) to make a short high sound","cn":"啁啾；吱吱叫","s":"The baby birds ________ loudly whenever their mother returns, and the loudest one usually gets fed first.","zh":"每當媽媽回來時，雛鳥就大聲吱吱叫，而叫得最大聲的那隻通常最先被餵食。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A148","t":"吱吱叫"},{"w":"howl","pos":"v.","def":"to make a long, loud crying sound","cn":"嚎叫","s":"Wolves ________ to call their pack together, and the sound can travel for many kilometres at night.","zh":"狼嚎叫來召集狼群，而這種聲音在夜晚可以傳到好幾公里遠。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A149","t":"嚎叫"},{"w":"growl","pos":"v.","def":"to make a low, angry sound in the throat","cn":"低吼","s":"The dog began to ________ when the stranger came near, so the man stepped back slowly.","zh":"當陌生人靠近時，那隻狗開始低吼，所以那個人慢慢地往後退。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A150","t":"低吼"},{"w":"purr","pos":"v.","def":"(of a cat) to make a soft, low sound when happy","cn":"呼嚕叫","s":"My cat likes to ________ on my lap in the evening, and the soft sound helps me relax after school.","zh":"我的貓喜歡晚上在我腿上呼嚕叫，而那柔和的聲音幫助我放學後放鬆。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A151","t":"呼嚕叫"},{"w":"hiss","pos":"v.","def":"to make a sound like a long \"sss\"","cn":"發出嘶嘶聲","s":"The snake began to ________ when we came close, so we quickly moved away from the rocks.","zh":"當我們靠近時那條蛇開始發出嘶嘶聲，所以我們迅速離開那些岩石。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A152","t":"發出嘶嘶聲"},{"w":"echolocation","pos":"n.","def":"finding objects by sending out sounds and hearing echoes","cn":"回聲定位","s":"Bats use ________ to catch insects in the dark, so they can hunt even when there is no moonlight.","zh":"蝙蝠利用回聲定位在黑暗中捕捉昆蟲，所以即使沒有月光牠們也能狩獵。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A153","t":"回聲定位"},{"w":"pheromone","pos":"n.","def":"a chemical an animal releases to send a message","cn":"費洛蒙","s":"Ants leave a ________ trail on the ground, and other ants follow it to find the food.","zh":"螞蟻在地上留下費洛蒙的足跡，而其他螞蟻會跟著它找到食物。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A154","t":"費洛蒙"},{"w":"scent","pos":"n.","def":"a smell, especially one left by an animal","cn":"氣味","s":"The tiger rubs its face on trees to leave its ________, and other tigers know to stay away.","zh":"老虎用臉磨蹭樹木留下牠的氣味，而其他老虎就知道要遠離。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A155","t":"氣味"},{"w":"body language","pos":"n.phr.","def":"messages sent by the way you move or stand","cn":"肢體語言","s":"A dog's ______ ______ tells you a lot, because a low tail and flat ears often mean it is afraid.","zh":"一隻狗的肢體語言能告訴你很多事，因為低垂的尾巴和平貼的耳朵通常表示牠很害怕。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A156","t":"肢體語言"},{"w":"alarm call","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a sound an animal makes to warn others of danger","cn":"警戒叫聲","s":"When a monkey sees an eagle, it gives a special ______ ______, and the whole group hides in the trees.","zh":"當一隻猴子看見老鷹時，牠會發出特別的警戒叫聲，而整個群體就躲進樹裡。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A157","t":"警戒叫聲"},{"w":"waggle dance","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a dance bees do to show where food is","cn":"搖擺舞","s":"A honeybee performs a ______ ______ inside the hive, and the other bees learn the direction of the flowers.","zh":"一隻蜜蜂在蜂巢內跳搖擺舞，而其他蜜蜂就知道花朵的方向。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A158","t":"搖擺舞"},{"w":"whisker","pos":"n.","def":"one of the long stiff hairs near an animal's mouth","cn":"鬍鬚","s":"A cat uses each ________ to measure narrow spaces, so you should never cut them off.","zh":"貓用每一根鬍鬚來測量狹窄的空間，所以你絕對不應該把它們剪掉。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A159","t":"鬍鬚"},{"w":"antenna","pos":"n.","def":"one of two long thin parts on an insect's head","cn":"觸角","s":"The ant touched the other ant with its ________, and in this way it could smell who belonged to its nest.","zh":"那隻螞蟻用觸角碰觸另一隻螞蟻，而藉此牠能聞出誰屬於牠的蟻巢。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A160","t":"觸角"},{"w":"wag","pos":"v.","def":"to move quickly from side to side","cn":"搖動（尾巴）","s":"Dogs usually ________ their tails when they are happy, but a stiff wagging tail can sometimes be a warning.","zh":"狗開心時通常會搖動尾巴，但僵硬地搖尾巴有時可能是一種警告。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A161","t":"搖動"},{"w":"threat display","pos":"n.phr.","def":"actions an animal uses to scare an enemy","cn":"威嚇展示","s":"The cat arched its back and made its fur stand up in a ______ ______, so the bigger dog decided to leave.","zh":"那隻貓拱起背、讓毛豎起來做出威嚇展示，所以那隻較大的狗決定離開。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A162","t":"威嚇展示"},{"w":"warning colours","pos":"n.phr.","def":"bright colours that tell enemies an animal is dangerous","cn":"警戒色","s":"Poison dart frogs have bright ______ ______, so birds learn quickly that these frogs are not safe to eat.","zh":"箭毒蛙有鮮豔的警戒色，所以鳥類很快就學會這些青蛙吃了不安全。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A163","t":"警戒色"},{"w":"play dead","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to lie still and pretend to be dead","cn":"裝死","s":"When a fox comes near, the opossum may ______ ______, and the fox often loses interest and walks away.","zh":"當狐狸靠近時，負鼠可能會裝死，而狐狸常常失去興趣然後走開。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A164","t":"裝死"},{"w":"migratory","pos":"adj.","def":"moving to another place each season","cn":"遷徙的","s":"Taiwan is an important stop for many ________ birds, and birdwatchers gather at the coast every autumn.","zh":"台灣是許多遷徙的鳥類的重要中途站，而賞鳥人士每年秋天都聚集在海岸邊。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A165","t":"遷徙的"},{"w":"homing","pos":"adj.","def":"able to find the way home from far away","cn":"歸巢的","s":"People once used ________ pigeons to carry messages, because the birds always returned to their own nests.","zh":"人們曾經利用歸巢的鴿子傳遞訊息，因為這些鳥總會回到自己的巢。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A166","t":"歸巢的"},{"w":"feral","pos":"adj.","def":"once tame but now living wild","cn":"野化的","s":"Many ________ cats live near the old market, and volunteers feed them and take them to the vet.","zh":"許多野化的貓住在舊市場附近，而志工們餵養牠們並帶牠們去看獸醫。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A167","t":"野化的"},{"w":"tool use","pos":"n.phr.","def":"using objects to help get food or do tasks","cn":"工具使用","s":"Sea otters break shells with stones, and this ______ ______ shows that clever behaviour is not only found in apes.","zh":"海獺用石頭敲開貝殼，而這種工具使用顯示聰明的行為不只出現在猿類身上。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A168","t":"工具使用"},{"w":"mirror test","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a test to see if an animal recognises itself in a mirror","cn":"鏡子測驗","s":"Elephants and dolphins have passed the ______ ______, so scientists believe they have some idea of who they are.","zh":"大象和海豚都通過了鏡子測驗，所以科學家相信牠們對自己是誰有某種概念。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A169","t":"鏡子測驗"},{"w":"parrot","pos":"n.","def":"a colourful bird that can copy human speech","cn":"鸚鵡","s":"My neighbour's ________ can say twenty words, and it always says hello when someone opens the door.","zh":"我鄰居的鸚鵡會說二十個字，而且每當有人開門時牠都會打招呼。","part":"A","sec":"Animal Behaviour & Communication 動物行為與溝通","lab":"A170","t":"鸚鵡"},{"w":"pack","pos":"n.","def":"a group of wolves or wild dogs","cn":"（狼）群","s":"A wolf ________ hunts together, so they can catch animals much larger than any single wolf.","zh":"一群狼會一起狩獵，所以牠們能捕捉比任何一隻狼都大得多的動物。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A171","t":"群"},{"w":"troop","pos":"n.","def":"a group of monkeys","cn":"（猴）群","s":"A ________ of monkeys stole the tourists' snacks, and the guide warned us to keep our bags closed.","zh":"一群猴子偷走了遊客的零食，而導遊警告我們要把包包關好。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A172","t":"群"},{"w":"pod","pos":"n.","def":"a group of whales or dolphins","cn":"（鯨豚）群","s":"We saw a ________ of dolphins from the boat, and they jumped beside us for almost ten minutes.","zh":"我們從船上看到一群海豚，而牠們在我們旁邊跳躍了將近十分鐘。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A173","t":"群"},{"w":"swarm","pos":"n.","def":"a large moving group of insects","cn":"（昆蟲）一大群","s":"A ________ of bees landed on the school gate, so the teachers kept the students inside until it left.","zh":"一大群蜜蜂停在學校大門上，所以老師們讓學生待在室內直到牠們離開。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A174","t":"大群"},{"w":"hive","pos":"n.","def":"a home where bees live together","cn":"蜂巢","s":"Each ________ has thousands of bees, but they all work together to collect food and protect the queen.","zh":"每個蜂巢裡有數千隻蜜蜂，但牠們全都一起合作採集食物並保護蜂后。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A175","t":"蜂巢"},{"w":"queen bee","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the only female bee in a hive that lays eggs","cn":"蜂后","s":"The ______ ______ can lay over a thousand eggs a day, while the worker bees feed her and clean the hive.","zh":"蜂后一天可以產下超過一千顆卵，而工蜂則餵養她並清潔蜂巢。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A176","t":"蜂后"},{"w":"worker ant","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an ant that collects food and builds the nest","cn":"工蟻","s":"Each ______ ______ can carry objects much heavier than itself, so a small group can move a whole dead insect.","zh":"每隻工蟻都能搬運比自己重得多的東西，所以一小群工蟻就能搬動一整隻死掉的昆蟲。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A177","t":"工蟻"},{"w":"termite","pos":"n.","def":"a small insect that eats wood and lives in large groups","cn":"白蟻","s":"________ in Africa build huge mounds of soil, and the tunnels inside keep the air cool.","zh":"非洲的白蟻會建造巨大的土丘，而裡面的通道讓空氣保持涼爽。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A178","t":"白蟻"},{"w":"alpha male","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the most powerful male in a group","cn":"首領雄性","s":"The ______ ______ eats first after a hunt, but he must also protect the group from danger.","zh":"首領雄性在狩獵後最先進食，但他也必須保護群體免受危險。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A179","t":"首領雄性"},{"w":"pecking order","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the order of rank within a group","cn":"啄序；等級次序","s":"The hens quickly formed a ______ ______, and the strongest hen always got the best place at the food bowl.","zh":"母雞們很快就形成了啄序，而最強壯的母雞總是在食盆旁佔到最好的位置。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A180","t":"啄序"},{"w":"grooming","pos":"n.","def":"cleaning another animal's fur","cn":"理毛","s":"Monkeys spend hours on ________ each day, and this helps them build friendships within the group.","zh":"猴子每天花好幾個小時理毛，而這幫助牠們在群體內建立友誼。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A181","t":"理毛"},{"w":"kin selection","pos":"n.phr.","def":"helping relatives so that shared genes survive","cn":"親屬選擇","s":"A bee may die to protect its hive, and scientists explain this with ______ ______, because the other bees are its sisters.","zh":"一隻蜜蜂可能會為了保護蜂巢而死，而科學家用親屬選擇來解釋這點，因為其他蜜蜂是牠的姊妹。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A182","t":"親屬選擇"},{"w":"cooperative","pos":"adj.","def":"working together with others","cn":"合作的","s":"Lions are ________ hunters, so they often surround a zebra from different sides before they attack.","zh":"獅子是合作的獵手，所以牠們常常在攻擊前從不同方向包圍一隻斑馬。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A183","t":"合作的"},{"w":"selfless","pos":"adj.","def":"caring more about others than yourself","cn":"無私的","s":"The mother bird made a ________ move when she pretended to be hurt, and the fox followed her away from the chicks.","zh":"母鳥假裝受傷，做出了無私的舉動，而狐狸跟著她離開了雛鳥。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A184","t":"無私的"},{"w":"freeloader","pos":"n.","def":"someone who takes help but gives nothing back","cn":"搭便車者；白吃白喝者","s":"In a vampire bat group, a ________ who never shares blood is soon ignored, so the bats rarely cheat.","zh":"在吸血蝠群體中，從不分享血液的搭便車者很快就會被冷落，所以蝙蝠很少作弊。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A185","t":"搭便車者"},{"w":"courtship","pos":"n.","def":"actions an animal uses to attract a partner","cn":"求偶","s":"The bird's ________ includes singing and dancing, and the female watches carefully before she chooses.","zh":"這種鳥的求偶包括唱歌和跳舞，而雌鳥在選擇之前會仔細觀察。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A186","t":"求偶"},{"w":"plumage","pos":"n.","def":"a bird's feathers","cn":"羽毛","s":"The male's bright ________ attracts females, but it also makes him easier for hawks to see.","zh":"雄鳥鮮豔的羽毛能吸引雌鳥，但也讓牠更容易被老鷹發現。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A187","t":"羽毛"},{"w":"peacock","pos":"n.","def":"a male bird with a large, colourful tail","cn":"雄孔雀","s":"The ________ spread his beautiful tail in the park, and a crowd of children gathered to take photos.","zh":"那隻雄孔雀在公園裡展開牠美麗的尾巴，而一群孩子聚集過來拍照。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A188","t":"雄孔雀"},{"w":"monogamous","pos":"adj.","def":"having only one partner","cn":"一夫一妻制的","s":"Swans are mostly ________, so a pair often stays together and raises chicks for many years.","zh":"天鵝大多是一夫一妻制的，所以一對天鵝常常會在一起並養育雛鳥好多年。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A189","t":"一夫一妻制的"},{"w":"pair bond","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a strong long-term link between two partners","cn":"配偶關係","s":"Penguins form a ______ ______ each season, and the parents call to each other to find their partner in the crowd.","zh":"企鵝每個季節都會建立配偶關係，而父母會互相呼叫，以便在擁擠的群體中找到伴侶。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A190","t":"配偶關係"},{"w":"brood","pos":"n.","def":"a group of young birds born at the same time","cn":"一窩幼鳥","s":"The duck led her ________ across the road, and the drivers stopped their cars to let them pass.","zh":"那隻鴨子帶著她的一窩幼鳥過馬路，而駕駛們停下車讓牠們通過。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A191","t":"一窩幼鳥"},{"w":"clutch","pos":"n.","def":"a group of eggs laid at one time","cn":"一窩蛋","s":"The turtle buried her ________ of eggs in the warm sand, and then she returned to the sea.","zh":"那隻海龜把她的一窩蛋埋在溫暖的沙子裡，然後回到海裡。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A192","t":"一窩蛋"},{"w":"chick","pos":"n.","def":"a baby bird","cn":"雛鳥；小雞","s":"The hungry ________ opened its mouth very wide, and its father pushed a small fish inside.","zh":"那隻飢餓的雛鳥把嘴張得很大，而牠的爸爸把一條小魚塞了進去。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A193","t":"雛鳥"},{"w":"parental care","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the ways parents look after their young","cn":"親代照顧","s":"Most fish give little ______ ______, but some male seahorses carry and protect the babies themselves.","zh":"大多數魚類很少提供親代照顧，但有些雄海馬會親自攜帶和保護寶寶。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A194","t":"親代照顧"},{"w":"nurse","pos":"v.","def":"to feed a baby with milk from its mother","cn":"哺乳","s":"The mother cat ________ her kittens every few hours, so she rarely leaves the box during the first week.","zh":"母貓每隔幾個小時就哺乳她的小貓，所以她在第一週很少離開箱子。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A195","t":"哺乳"},{"w":"vampire bat","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a bat that feeds on the blood of animals","cn":"吸血蝙蝠","s":"A hungry ______ ______ can die after two nights without food, so friends share their meals to keep each other alive.","zh":"一隻飢餓的吸血蝙蝠兩晚沒有進食就可能死亡，所以朋友之間會分享食物讓彼此活下去。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A196","t":"吸血蝙蝠"},{"w":"meerkat","pos":"n.","def":"a small African animal that stands on its back legs","cn":"狐獴","s":"One ________ stands on a rock to watch for eagles, while the others dig for insects in the sand.","zh":"一隻狐獴站在岩石上留意老鷹，而其他狐獴在沙地裡挖昆蟲。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A197","t":"狐獴"},{"w":"lookout","pos":"n.","def":"an animal or person who watches for danger","cn":"守望者；哨兵","s":"The goose that acts as a ________ keeps its head up, and it honks loudly if a dog comes near.","zh":"擔任守望者的那隻鵝會抬著頭，而如果有狗靠近牠就會大聲鳴叫。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A198","t":"守望者"},{"w":"matriarch","pos":"n.","def":"an old female who leads a family group","cn":"女族長","s":"The elephant ________ remembers where water can be found, so the group follows her during dry seasons.","zh":"象群的女族長記得哪裡可以找到水，所以群體在乾季會跟隨她。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A199","t":"女族長"},{"w":"division of labour","pos":"n.phr.","def":"splitting work so each member does a different job","cn":"分工","s":"Ant colonies have a clear ______ ______ ______, because some ants find food while others care for the young.","zh":"蟻群有明確的分工，因為有些螞蟻尋找食物，而其他螞蟻照顧幼蟲。","part":"A","sec":"Social Life, Mating & Parenting 社會生活、求偶與育幼","lab":"A200","t":"分工"},{"w":"analysis","pos":"n.","def":"a careful study of something to understand it","cn":"分析","s":"The lab's ________ of the bones showed that the animal was young, so it probably died before it could have babies.","zh":"實驗室對骨頭的分析顯示這隻動物很年輕，所以牠很可能在生育之前就死了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B1","t":"分析"},{"w":"prediction","pos":"n.","def":"a statement about what will happen","cn":"預測","s":"Darwin made a ________ about a moth with a very long tongue, and scientists finally found it forty years later.","zh":"達爾文對一種舌頭極長的蛾做出了預測，而科學家終於在四十年後找到了牠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B2","t":"預測"},{"w":"approximation","pos":"n.","def":"a number or idea that is close but not exact","cn":"近似值；概算","s":"Six million years is only an ________, because scientists cannot know exactly when humans and chimps split.","zh":"六百萬年只是一個近似值，因為科學家無法確切知道人類和黑猩猩是何時分開的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B3","t":"近似值"},{"w":"concentrate","pos":"v.","def":"to give all your attention to something","cn":"專注","s":"The cat seemed to ________ completely on the mouse hole, and it did not move for almost an hour.","zh":"那隻貓似乎完全專注在老鼠洞上，而且牠幾乎一個小時都沒有動。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B4","t":"專注"},{"w":"essence","pos":"n.","def":"the most important basic quality of something","cn":"本質；精髓","s":"The ________ of Darwin's idea is simple, but it took him more than twenty years to publish it.","zh":"達爾文想法的本質很簡單，但他花了二十多年才把它發表出來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B5","t":"本質"},{"w":"activate","pos":"v.","def":"to make something start working","cn":"啟動；活化","s":"Sunlight can ________ certain genes in your skin, so your skin becomes darker after a summer holiday.","zh":"陽光能活化你皮膚中的某些基因，所以暑假過後你的皮膚會變得比較黑。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B6","t":"活化"},{"w":"capture","pos":"v.","def":"to catch an animal or person","cn":"捕捉","s":"The team used soft nets to ________ the birds, and they released them after putting small rings on their legs.","zh":"研究團隊用柔軟的網子捕捉鳥類，並在牠們腳上套上小環後把牠們放走。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B7","t":"捕捉"},{"w":"circumstantial","pos":"adj.","def":"suggesting something but not proving it directly","cn":"間接的；旁證的","s":"The evidence against the dog was only ________, because nobody actually saw it eat the cake.","zh":"對那隻狗不利的證據只是間接的，因為沒有人真的看見牠吃了蛋糕。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B8","t":"間接的"},{"w":"conditional","pos":"adj.","def":"depending on something else happening","cn":"有條件的","s":"The monkey's help was ________, so it only shared food with monkeys that had shared with it before.","zh":"那隻猴子的幫忙是有條件的，所以牠只和以前跟牠分享過食物的猴子分享。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B9","t":"有條件的"},{"w":"contextual","pos":"adj.","def":"depending on the situation around something","cn":"情境的；與上下文有關的","s":"Students used ________ clues to guess the meaning of \"gene pool\", and most of them guessed correctly.","zh":"學生利用上下文的線索猜出「基因庫」的意思，而大多數人都猜對了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B10","t":"上下文的"},{"w":"debunk","pos":"v.","def":"to show that a popular belief is false","cn":"揭穿；駁斥","s":"Our teacher wanted to ________ the myth that goldfish only remember things for three seconds, so she showed us a study.","zh":"我們老師想要駁斥金魚只有三秒記憶的迷思，所以她給我們看了一項研究。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B11","t":"駁斥"},{"w":"exterminate","pos":"v.","def":"to kill all of a group of animals","cn":"撲滅；滅絕","s":"The city decided to ________ the rats near the market, but some people asked for a kinder solution.","zh":"市政府決定撲滅市場附近的老鼠，但有些人要求更溫和的解決辦法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B12","t":"撲滅"},{"w":"foreshadow","pos":"v.","def":"to show signs of something that will happen later","cn":"預示","s":"Small changes in the birds' songs may ________ the birth of a new species, although it could take thousands of years.","zh":"鳥鳴中的小變化可能預示一個新物種的誕生，雖然這可能需要數千年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B13","t":"預示"},{"w":"implicate","pos":"v.","def":"to show that something is involved in a problem","cn":"牽涉；顯示與…有關","s":"The study seemed to ________ one gene in the disease, but the scientists said more tests were needed.","zh":"這項研究似乎顯示一個基因與這種疾病有關，但科學家說還需要更多測試。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B14","t":"有關"},{"w":"interfere","pos":"v.","def":"to get involved and cause problems","cn":"干擾","s":"Tourists should not ________ with nesting turtles, because bright lights and noise can scare them back into the sea.","zh":"遊客不應該干擾正在築巢的海龜，因為強光和噪音會把牠們嚇回海裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B15","t":"干擾"},{"w":"intertwine","pos":"v.","def":"to twist or link closely together","cn":"交織；緊密相連","s":"Genes and environment ________ in complex ways, so it is hard to say which one matters more.","zh":"基因和環境以複雜的方式交織在一起，所以很難說哪一個更重要。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B16","t":"交織"},{"w":"invalidate","pos":"v.","def":"to show that something is not correct","cn":"使無效；推翻","s":"One mistake in the data could ________ the whole study, so the scientists checked every number twice.","zh":"資料中的一個錯誤就可能推翻整個研究，所以科學家把每個數字都檢查了兩次。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B17","t":"推翻"},{"w":"moderate","pos":"adj.","def":"not too much and not too little","cn":"適度的；中等的","s":"The plants grew best at ________ temperatures, but they died quickly when the greenhouse became too hot.","zh":"這些植物在適度的溫度下長得最好，但當溫室變得太熱時它們很快就死了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B18","t":"適度的"},{"w":"neutralise","pos":"v.","def":"to stop something from having an effect","cn":"中和；使失效","s":"Some animals such as the mongoose can ________ snake poison, so they can eat snakes without getting sick.","zh":"有些像獴這樣的動物能中和蛇毒，所以牠們可以吃蛇而不會生病。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B19","t":"中和"},{"w":"reaffirm","pos":"v.","def":"to say again that something is true","cn":"重申；再次確認","s":"The new fossils ________ the idea that birds came from dinosaurs, and few scientists now doubt it.","zh":"新的化石再次確認了鳥類來自恐龍的觀點，而現在很少有科學家懷疑這一點。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B20","t":"再次確認"},{"w":"sever","pos":"v.","def":"to cut or break completely","cn":"切斷","s":"The new highway may ________ the path that the frogs use every spring, so the city built small tunnels under the road.","zh":"新的高速公路可能會切斷青蛙每年春天使用的路徑，所以市政府在路下方建造了小隧道。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B21","t":"切斷"},{"w":"shed / shed / shed","pos":"v.","def":"to lose skin, hair or leaves naturally","cn":"脫落；蛻（皮）","s":"Snakes ________ their skin several times a year, and you can sometimes find the old skin in the grass.","zh":"蛇每年會蛻皮好幾次，而你有時可以在草叢裡找到舊的蛇皮。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B22","t":"蛻"},{"w":"stabilise","pos":"v.","def":"to become steady and stop changing","cn":"穩定下來","s":"The number of deer began to ________ after wolves returned, and the forest plants slowly grew back.","zh":"狼回來之後鹿的數量開始穩定下來，而森林裡的植物也慢慢長了回來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B23","t":"穩定下來"},{"w":"symbolise","pos":"v.","def":"to be a sign of an idea","cn":"象徵","s":"In many cultures, the owl is used to ________ wisdom, although owls are not cleverer than many other birds.","zh":"在許多文化中，貓頭鷹被用來象徵智慧，雖然貓頭鷹並沒有比許多其他鳥類更聰明。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B24","t":"象徵"},{"w":"initial","pos":"adj.","def":"happening at the beginning","cn":"最初的","s":"The ________ results looked exciting, but later tests showed that the gene had only a small effect.","zh":"最初的結果看起來令人興奮，但後來的測試顯示這個基因只有很小的影響。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B25","t":"最初的"},{"w":"anatomy","pos":"n.","def":"the structure of a body","cn":"解剖構造；解剖學","s":"A bat's wing and a human hand have a similar ________, because both contain the same kinds of bones.","zh":"蝙蝠的翅膀和人類的手有相似的解剖構造，因為兩者都包含相同種類的骨頭。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B26","t":"解剖構造"},{"w":"archetype","pos":"n.","def":"a perfect typical example of something","cn":"典型；原型","s":"The lion is the ________ of a powerful hunter in stories, but in real life the females do most of the hunting.","zh":"獅子在故事中是強大獵手的典型，但在現實生活中大部分的狩獵是母獅做的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B27","t":"典型"},{"w":"bearing","pos":"n.","def":"influence or connection","cn":"關係；影響","s":"Your diet as a child may have a ________ on your health as an adult, so parents should offer healthy meals.","zh":"你小時候的飲食可能對你成年後的健康有影響，所以父母應該提供健康的餐點。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B28","t":"影響"},{"w":"chaos","pos":"n.","def":"a state of complete confusion","cn":"混亂","s":"The fox ran into the chicken house, and there was ________ as the birds flew in every direction.","zh":"狐狸衝進雞舍，而雞群向四面八方飛竄，一片混亂。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B29","t":"混亂"},{"w":"collaboration","pos":"n.","def":"working together with others","cn":"合作","s":"The project was a ________ between scientists from twenty countries, and they shared all their data online.","zh":"這個計畫是來自二十個國家科學家之間的合作，而他們在網路上分享所有的資料。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B30","t":"合作"},{"w":"conclusion","pos":"n.","def":"a decision you reach after thinking","cn":"結論","s":"After watching the crows for months, she came to the ________ that they could recognise human faces.","zh":"觀察烏鴉好幾個月之後，她得出了牠們能認出人臉的結論。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B31","t":"結論"},{"w":"derivative","pos":"n.","def":"something developed from something else","cn":"衍生物","s":"Aspirin is a ________ of a chemical found in tree bark, and people used the bark as medicine long ago.","zh":"阿斯匹靈是樹皮中一種化學物質的衍生物，而人們很久以前就把樹皮當作藥使用。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B32","t":"衍生物"},{"w":"exception","pos":"n.","def":"something that does not follow the usual rule","cn":"例外","s":"Most mammals do not lay eggs, but the platypus is an ________, and that surprised early scientists.","zh":"大多數哺乳類動物不會下蛋，但鴨嘴獸是例外，而這讓早期的科學家很驚訝。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B33","t":"例外"},{"w":"fidelity","pos":"n.","def":"loyalty to a partner","cn":"忠誠","s":"Scientists once praised the ________ of swans, but DNA tests showed that some chicks have a different father.","zh":"科學家曾經讚揚天鵝的忠誠，但DNA檢測顯示有些雛鳥的父親是另一隻。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B34","t":"忠誠"},{"w":"flaw","pos":"n.","def":"a mistake or weakness","cn":"缺陷；瑕疵","s":"There was a ________ in the experiment, because the scientists forgot to give one group of mice the same food.","zh":"這個實驗有一個缺陷，因為科學家忘了給其中一組老鼠吃同樣的食物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B35","t":"缺陷"},{"w":"hindrance","pos":"n.","def":"something that makes progress difficult","cn":"阻礙","s":"A heavy tail can be a ________ when a bird escapes from a predator, but it helps the bird attract a mate.","zh":"沉重的尾巴在鳥逃離掠食者時可能是一種阻礙，但它能幫助鳥吸引配偶。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B36","t":"阻礙"},{"w":"inclusion","pos":"n.","def":"adding someone or something to a group","cn":"納入；包含","s":"The ________ of more women in the study was important, because earlier results were based mostly on men.","zh":"在研究中納入更多女性很重要，因為先前的結果主要是基於男性。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B37","t":"納入"},{"w":"inquiry","pos":"n.","def":"an official question or investigation","cn":"調查；詢問","s":"The university started an ________ into the lab, because some results seemed too perfect to be true.","zh":"大學對這間實驗室展開了調查，因為有些結果看起來完美得令人難以置信。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B38","t":"調查"},{"w":"manifestation","pos":"n.","def":"a sign that shows something exists","cn":"表現；顯現","s":"Tail wagging is one ________ of a dog's mood, but you should also watch its ears and eyes.","zh":"搖尾巴是狗的情緒的一種表現，但你也應該觀察牠的耳朵和眼睛。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B39","t":"表現"},{"w":"narrative","pos":"n.","def":"a story or explanation of events","cn":"敘事；說法","s":"The old ________ said humans left Africa only once, but new DNA evidence tells a more complex story.","zh":"舊的說法認為人類只離開非洲一次，但新的DNA證據講述了一個更複雜的故事。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B40","t":"說法"},{"w":"rebuttal","pos":"n.","def":"an answer that shows something is wrong","cn":"反駁","s":"The young scientist wrote a ________ to the article, and she used her own data to show its mistakes.","zh":"那位年輕的科學家針對這篇文章寫了一篇反駁，而她用自己的資料指出文章的錯誤。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B41","t":"反駁"},{"w":"repertoire","pos":"n.","def":"all the things a person or animal can do","cn":"全部本領；曲目","s":"A mockingbird has a huge ________ of songs, and it can even copy car alarms and phones.","zh":"一隻嘲鶇擁有大量的曲目，而牠甚至能模仿汽車警報器和電話的聲音。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B42","t":"曲目"},{"w":"scepticism","pos":"n.","def":"doubt about whether something is true","cn":"懷疑態度","s":"Many people met the idea of talking dolphins with ________, because the early studies were very small.","zh":"許多人以懷疑態度看待會說話的海豚這種想法，因為早期的研究規模很小。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B43","t":"懷疑態度"},{"w":"subset","pos":"n.","def":"a smaller group within a larger group","cn":"子集；一部分","s":"Only a small ________ of the birds learned the new song, but those birds attracted more females.","zh":"只有一小部分的鳥學會了新的歌曲，但那些鳥吸引了更多雌鳥。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B44","t":"部分"},{"w":"terminology","pos":"n.","def":"special words used in a subject","cn":"術語","s":"Genetics has a lot of difficult ________, so our teacher gave us a word list before the lesson.","zh":"遺傳學有很多困難的術語，所以我們老師在上課前給了我們一張單字表。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B45","t":"術語"},{"w":"tolerance","pos":"n.","def":"the ability to accept or survive something","cn":"耐受力；容忍","s":"Some adults have no ________ for milk, because their bodies stop making the enzyme after childhood.","zh":"有些成年人對牛奶沒有耐受力，因為他們的身體在童年後就不再製造那種酵素。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B46","t":"耐受力"},{"w":"accidental","pos":"adj.","def":"happening by chance","cn":"意外的","s":"The discovery was ________, because the scientist was studying something else when she noticed the glowing cells.","zh":"這個發現是意外的，因為那位科學家注意到發光細胞時正在研究別的東西。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B47","t":"意外的"},{"w":"asymmetrical","pos":"adj.","def":"having two sides that are not the same","cn":"不對稱的","s":"Some owls have ________ ears, so they can tell exactly where a sound comes from in the dark.","zh":"有些貓頭鷹的耳朵是不對稱的，所以牠們能在黑暗中精確分辨聲音從哪裡傳來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B48","t":"不對稱的"},{"w":"deficient","pos":"adj.","def":"not having enough of something","cn":"缺乏的","s":"The puppies were ________ in vitamins, so the vet changed their food and they soon became stronger.","zh":"那些小狗缺乏維生素，所以獸醫換了牠們的食物，而牠們很快就變得更強壯。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B49","t":"缺乏"},{"w":"faulty","pos":"adj.","def":"not working correctly","cn":"有缺陷的；故障的","s":"A ________ gene can cause a serious illness, but sometimes doctors can treat it with new medicines.","zh":"一個有缺陷的基因可能導致嚴重的疾病，但有時醫生可以用新藥治療。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B50","t":"有缺陷的"},{"w":"functional","pos":"adj.","def":"working and useful","cn":"有功能的","s":"Ostriches have wings, but they are not ________ for flying, so the birds use them for balance instead.","zh":"鴕鳥有翅膀，但它們不是有功能的飛行翅膀，所以鴕鳥改用翅膀來保持平衡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B51","t":"有功能的"},{"w":"genuine","pos":"adj.","def":"real and true","cn":"真正的","s":"The dog showed ________ fear during the storm, so we let it sleep inside the house with us.","zh":"那隻狗在暴風雨中表現出真正的恐懼，所以我們讓牠和我們一起睡在屋子裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B52","t":"真正的"},{"w":"identifiable","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be recognised","cn":"可辨認的","s":"Each zebra is ________ by its stripes, because no two zebras have exactly the same pattern.","zh":"每隻斑馬都可以藉由牠的條紋辨認出來，因為沒有兩隻斑馬的花紋完全相同。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B53","t":"辨認"},{"w":"illogical","pos":"adj.","def":"not sensible or reasonable","cn":"不合邏輯的","s":"It seems ________ for a bird to carry such a heavy tail, but the tail helps it win a partner.","zh":"一隻鳥背負這麼沉重的尾巴似乎不合邏輯，但這條尾巴幫助牠贏得伴侶。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B54","t":"不合邏輯"},{"w":"immune","pos":"adj.","def":"not able to be affected by a disease","cn":"免疫的","s":"Some people are ________ to the virus, because they carry a rare gene that blocks it.","zh":"有些人對這種病毒是免疫的，因為他們帶有一個能阻擋病毒的罕見基因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B55","t":"免疫的"},{"w":"independent","pos":"adj.","def":"not needing help from others","cn":"獨立的","s":"Young sea turtles are ________ from the moment they hatch, so they must reach the sea without help.","zh":"小海龜從孵化的那一刻起就是獨立的，所以牠們必須在沒有幫助的情況下抵達大海。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B56","t":"獨立的"},{"w":"influential","pos":"adj.","def":"having a strong effect on others","cn":"有影響力的","s":"Darwin's book was very ________, and it changed the way people thought about nature and themselves.","zh":"達爾文的書非常有影響力，而它改變了人們對大自然和自身的看法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B57","t":"有影響力"},{"w":"irrelevant","pos":"adj.","def":"not connected to the subject","cn":"無關的","s":"The colour of a dog's fur is ________ to its intelligence, so you cannot judge a dog by its coat.","zh":"狗的毛色與牠的聰明程度無關，所以你不能以毛色來評斷一隻狗。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B58","t":"無關"},{"w":"partial","pos":"adj.","def":"not complete","cn":"部分的","s":"The scientists found only a ________ skeleton, but it was enough to show that the animal walked on two legs.","zh":"科學家只找到了一副部分的骨骼，但這足以顯示這隻動物用兩條腿走路。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B59","t":"部分的"},{"w":"persistent","pos":"adj.","def":"continuing for a long time","cn":"持續的；堅持不懈的","s":"The ________ crow tried again and again to open the box, and finally it worked out how to lift the lid.","zh":"那隻堅持不懈的烏鴉一次又一次地嘗試打開箱子，最後牠想出了如何掀開蓋子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B60","t":"堅持不懈的"},{"w":"restrictive","pos":"adj.","def":"limiting what people can do","cn":"限制性的","s":"Some countries have very ________ laws on gene editing, but others allow scientists to do much more research.","zh":"有些國家對基因編輯有非常限制性的法律，但其他國家允許科學家進行更多研究。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B61","t":"限制性的"},{"w":"static","pos":"adj.","def":"not moving or changing","cn":"靜止的；不變的","s":"People once thought species were ________, but Darwin showed that they change slowly over time.","zh":"人們曾經認為物種是不變的，但達爾文證明了它們會隨著時間慢慢改變。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B62","t":"不變的"},{"w":"unbiased","pos":"adj.","def":"fair and not influenced by personal opinions","cn":"不偏不倚的","s":"Scientists try to be ________ when they watch animals, but it is easy to see human feelings where there are none.","zh":"科學家觀察動物時盡量保持不偏不倚，但很容易在沒有人類情感的地方看到人類情感。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B63","t":"不偏不倚"},{"w":"unreliable","pos":"adj.","def":"not able to be trusted","cn":"不可靠的","s":"Some cheap DNA tests are ________, so you should not make health decisions based on them alone.","zh":"有些便宜的DNA檢測是不可靠的，所以你不應該只根據它們做健康方面的決定。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B64","t":"不可靠的"},{"w":"subsequently","pos":"adv.","def":"after something else happened","cn":"隨後","s":"The lab first tested the drug on mice, and they ________ tested it on a small group of volunteers.","zh":"實驗室先在老鼠身上測試這種藥物，而他們隨後又在一小群志願者身上進行測試。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B65","t":"隨後"},{"w":"widely","pos":"adv.","def":"by many people or in many places","cn":"廣泛地","s":"Darwin's theory is now ________ accepted, but it caused angry arguments when it was first published.","zh":"達爾文的理論現在被廣泛地接受，但它首次發表時曾引起激烈的爭論。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B66","t":"廣泛地"},{"w":"inherently","pos":"adv.","def":"as a basic, natural part of something","cn":"本質上；天生地","s":"Wolves are not ________ dangerous to people, but they may attack when they are very hungry or afraid.","zh":"狼本質上對人類並不危險，但牠們在非常飢餓或害怕時可能會攻擊。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B67","t":"本質上"},{"w":"progressively","pos":"adv.","def":"gradually, step by step","cn":"逐步地","s":"The fish's fins became ________ stronger over millions of years, and finally they could support its body on land.","zh":"經過數百萬年，這種魚的鰭逐步地變得更強壯，最後它們能在陸地上支撐牠的身體。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B68","t":"逐步地"},{"w":"intentionally","pos":"adv.","def":"on purpose","cn":"故意地","s":"The bird ________ dropped the nut onto the road, and it waited for a car to crack the shell.","zh":"那隻鳥故意地把堅果丟到馬路上，然後等待汽車把殼壓碎。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B69","t":"故意地"},{"w":"collectively","pos":"adv.","def":"as a group","cn":"集體地","s":"The fish move ________ in a large school, so a shark finds it hard to focus on just one.","zh":"魚群以大群集體地移動，所以鯊魚很難只專注在其中一條魚上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B70","t":"集體地"},{"w":"partly","pos":"adv.","def":"to some degree, but not completely","cn":"部分地","s":"Your height is ________ decided by your genes, but good food and enough sleep also help you grow.","zh":"你的身高部分由基因決定，但良好的食物和充足的睡眠也能幫助你長高。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B71","t":"部分"},{"w":"typically","pos":"adv.","def":"usually","cn":"通常","s":"Female cats ________ have four to six kittens, and the mother looks after them for about two months.","zh":"母貓通常會生四到六隻小貓，而貓媽媽會照顧牠們大約兩個月。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B72","t":"通常"},{"w":"frequently","pos":"adv.","def":"often","cn":"經常","s":"Dolphins ________ help each other when one is hurt, and they lift the injured dolphin to the surface to breathe.","zh":"當一隻海豚受傷時，海豚們經常互相幫助，而且牠們會把受傷的海豚托到水面呼吸。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B73","t":"經常"},{"w":"therefore","pos":"adv.","def":"for that reason","cn":"因此","s":"The two birds cannot produce young together, and ________ scientists classify them as separate species.","zh":"這兩種鳥無法一起生下後代，因此科學家把牠們歸類為不同的物種。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B74","t":"因此"},{"w":"mutually","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that helps or affects both sides","cn":"互相地","s":"The small fish clean the shark's teeth and get a free meal, so the relationship is ________ helpful.","zh":"小魚清潔鯊魚的牙齒並得到一頓免費的餐點，所以這種關係是互相有益的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B75","t":"互相"},{"w":"statistically","pos":"adv.","def":"according to numbers and data","cn":"統計上","s":"The difference between the two groups was not ________ important, so the scientists could not support their idea.","zh":"兩組之間的差異在統計上並不顯著，所以科學家無法支持他們的想法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B76","t":"統計上"},{"w":"uniquely","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that no other thing has","cn":"獨特地","s":"Humans are ________ good at learning languages, but many animals also communicate in surprising ways.","zh":"人類在學習語言方面獨特地擅長，但許多動物也以令人驚訝的方式溝通。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B77","t":"獨特地"},{"w":"sharply","pos":"adv.","def":"suddenly and by a large amount","cn":"急劇地","s":"The number of bees fell ________ last year, and farmers worried about their fruit trees.","zh":"蜜蜂的數量去年急劇地下降，而農民們擔心他們的果樹。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B78","t":"急劇地"},{"w":"drastically","pos":"adv.","def":"in a sudden and extreme way","cn":"大幅地；劇烈地","s":"The cost of reading DNA has fallen ________, so many hospitals can now test patients' genes.","zh":"讀取DNA的成本已經大幅地下降，所以現在許多醫院都能檢測病人的基因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B79","t":"大幅地"},{"w":"conceptualise","pos":"v.","def":"to form an idea of something in your mind","cn":"構想；概念化","s":"It is hard to ________ how long four billion years is, so our teacher compared Earth's history to a single day.","zh":"很難構想四十億年有多長，所以我們老師把地球的歷史比喻成一天。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B80","t":"構想"},{"w":"construe","pos":"v.","def":"to understand something in a certain way","cn":"理解；解讀","s":"People often ________ a chimp's wide smile as happiness, but it usually means the animal is afraid.","zh":"人們常常把黑猩猩咧嘴的笑容解讀為快樂，但那通常表示這隻動物很害怕。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B81","t":"解讀"},{"w":"deceive","pos":"v.","def":"to make someone believe something false","cn":"欺騙","s":"Some birds ________ their enemies by pretending to have a broken wing, and they lead the danger away from the nest.","zh":"有些鳥會假裝翅膀受傷來欺騙牠們的敵人，並把危險引離巢穴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B82","t":"欺騙"},{"w":"differ","pos":"v.","def":"to be not the same","cn":"不同","s":"Human DNA does not ________ much from person to person, so we are all more alike than we think.","zh":"人類的DNA在人與人之間並沒有太大的不同，所以我們彼此比自己想像的更相似。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B83","t":"不同"},{"w":"disprove","pos":"v.","def":"to show that something is not true","cn":"證明…是錯的","s":"The experiment was designed to ________ the old belief, and the results clearly showed that it was wrong.","zh":"這個實驗是為了證明那個舊觀念是錯的而設計的，而結果清楚地顯示它確實錯了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B84","t":"證明 是錯的"},{"w":"duplicate","pos":"v.","def":"to make an exact copy","cn":"複製","s":"Before a cell divides, it must ________ its DNA, so each new cell gets a full set of instructions.","zh":"細胞在分裂之前必須複製它的DNA，這樣每個新細胞才能得到一整套指令。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B85","t":"複製"},{"w":"elapse","pos":"v.","def":"(of time) to pass","cn":"（時間）流逝","s":"Millions of years must ________ before a new species forms, so we rarely see it happen in our lifetime.","zh":"必須流逝數百萬年才會形成一個新物種，所以我們很少在一生中看到它發生。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B86","t":"流逝"},{"w":"enrich","pos":"v.","def":"to improve the quality of something","cn":"豐富；充實","s":"Zoos ________ the lives of their animals with toys and puzzles, because bored animals can become stressed.","zh":"動物園用玩具和益智遊戲來豐富動物的生活，因為無聊的動物會變得有壓力。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B87","t":"豐富"},{"w":"favour","pos":"v.","def":"to give an advantage to","cn":"有利於；偏好","s":"Cold weather tends to ________ animals with thick fur, so mammals in the far north are usually furry.","zh":"寒冷的天氣往往有利於毛皮厚的動物，所以極北地區的哺乳類通常都毛茸茸的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B88","t":"有利於"},{"w":"infest","pos":"v.","def":"(of insects or animals) to fill a place in large numbers","cn":"大批出沒；侵擾","s":"Fleas can ________ a house very quickly, so pet owners should check their animals regularly.","zh":"跳蚤能很快地侵擾一間房子，所以寵物主人應該定期檢查他們的動物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B89","t":"侵擾"},{"w":"possess","pos":"v.","def":"to have or own","cn":"擁有","s":"Many birds ________ a kind of compass in their eyes, and this helps them find their way across oceans.","zh":"許多鳥類眼中擁有一種指南針，而這幫助牠們找到橫越海洋的路。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B90","t":"擁有"},{"w":"secrete","pos":"v.","def":"to produce a liquid inside the body","cn":"分泌","s":"Frogs ________ a slimy liquid from their skin, and it keeps them wet and protects them from germs.","zh":"青蛙從皮膚分泌一種黏滑的液體，而它能保持牠們濕潤並保護牠們免受細菌感染。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B91","t":"分泌"},{"w":"alternate","pos":"v.","def":"to take turns or change between two things","cn":"輪流；交替","s":"The two parent birds ________ between sitting on the eggs and looking for food, so the eggs are never left cold.","zh":"兩隻親鳥輪流孵蛋和尋找食物，所以蛋從來不會被留著變冷。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B92","t":"輪流"},{"w":"arouse","pos":"v.","def":"to cause a feeling or reaction","cn":"引起；激起","s":"The strange noise ________ the dog's curiosity, so it walked slowly towards the bushes to find out more.","zh":"那奇怪的聲音激起了狗的好奇心，所以牠慢慢走向灌木叢想一探究竟。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B93","t":"激起"},{"w":"attach","pos":"v.","def":"to fix or join one thing to another","cn":"附著；貼上","s":"Scientists ________ tiny trackers to the turtles' shells, and they can follow the animals across the ocean.","zh":"科學家把小型追蹤器貼在海龜殼上，而他們就能追蹤這些動物橫越海洋。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B94","t":"貼"},{"w":"attract","pos":"v.","def":"to make something come closer","cn":"吸引","s":"Male frogs sing loudly to ________ females, but the noise can also bring hungry bats.","zh":"雄蛙大聲鳴叫以吸引雌蛙，但這噪音也可能招來飢餓的蝙蝠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B95","t":"吸引"},{"w":"compete","pos":"v.","def":"to try to win against others","cn":"競爭","s":"Young male deer ________ for the attention of females, and the winners are usually the largest ones.","zh":"年輕的雄鹿為了吸引雌鹿的注意而競爭，而勝利者通常是體型最大的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B96","t":"競爭"},{"w":"determine","pos":"v.","def":"to decide or find out exactly","cn":"決定；確定","s":"In some turtles, the sand temperature can ________ whether a baby is male or female.","zh":"在某些海龜中，沙子的溫度能決定寶寶是雄性還是雌性。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B97","t":"決定"},{"w":"distract","pos":"v.","def":"to take someone's attention away","cn":"使分心","s":"The mother bird flies around noisily to ________ the cat, while her chicks hide quietly in the nest.","zh":"母鳥吵鬧地四處飛來使那隻貓分心，而她的雛鳥安靜地躲在巢裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B98","t":"使 分心"},{"w":"foresee / foresaw / foreseen","pos":"v.","def":"to know that something will happen","cn":"預見","s":"Few scientists could ________ how quickly gene editing would develop, and now laws are struggling to keep up.","zh":"很少有科學家能預見基因編輯會發展得這麼快，而現在法律正努力追趕。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B99","t":"預見"},{"w":"recognise","pos":"v.","def":"to know someone or something you have seen before","cn":"認出","s":"Sheep can ________ the faces of other sheep, and they can remember them for up to two years.","zh":"羊能認出其他羊的臉，而且牠們能記住長達兩年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B100","t":"認出"},{"w":"regard","pos":"v.","def":"to think of in a particular way","cn":"視為；認為","s":"Many farmers ________ crows as pests, but scientists see them as some of the cleverest birds on Earth.","zh":"許多農民把烏鴉視為害鳥，但科學家把牠們看作地球上最聰明的鳥類之一。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B101","t":"視為"},{"w":"relate","pos":"v.","def":"to find or show a connection","cn":"有關聯；與…相關","s":"Scientists are trying to ________ certain genes to sleep habits, because some people need much less sleep than others.","zh":"科學家正試著把某些基因與睡眠習慣相關聯，因為有些人需要的睡眠比別人少得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B102","t":"相關聯"},{"w":"simplify","pos":"v.","def":"to make something easier to understand","cn":"簡化","s":"The teacher tried to ________ the topic of DNA, so she compared it to a recipe book in a kitchen.","zh":"老師試著簡化DNA這個主題，所以她把它比喻成廚房裡的食譜書。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B103","t":"簡化"},{"w":"anthropomorphism","pos":"n.","def":"giving human feelings to animals or objects","cn":"擬人化","s":"Saying your dog feels guilty may be ________, because it might simply be reacting to your angry voice.","zh":"說你的狗感到內疚可能是擬人化，因為牠可能只是對你生氣的聲音做出反應。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B104","t":"擬人化"},{"w":"immutable","pos":"adj.","def":"never changing","cn":"不可改變的","s":"Our genes are not completely ________, because small mutations happen almost every time our cells divide.","zh":"我們的基因並非完全不可改變的，因為幾乎每次我們的細胞分裂時都會發生小突變。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B105","t":"不可改變的"},{"w":"inadequate","pos":"adj.","def":"not good enough","cn":"不足的；不充分的","s":"The cage was ________ for such a large bird, so the rescue centre moved it to an outdoor area.","zh":"那個籠子對這麼大的鳥來說是不足的，所以救援中心把牠移到戶外區域。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B106","t":"不足的"},{"w":"inconspicuous","pos":"adj.","def":"not easily seen or noticed","cn":"不顯眼的","s":"Female ducks are brown and ________, so they can sit on their nests without being seen by foxes.","zh":"雌鴨是褐色而且不顯眼的，所以牠們能坐在巢上而不被狐狸看見。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B107","t":"不顯眼的"},{"w":"indistinguishable","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to tell apart","cn":"無法區分的","s":"The two species of mosquito are almost ________, but only one of them carries the disease.","zh":"這兩種蚊子幾乎是無法區分的，但只有其中一種會傳播疾病。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B108","t":"無法區分的"},{"w":"irrefutable","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to prove wrong","cn":"無可辯駁的","s":"The DNA evidence was ________, so the man finally admitted that he was the child's father.","zh":"DNA證據是無可辯駁的，所以那名男子最終承認他是孩子的父親。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B109","t":"無可辯駁的"},{"w":"misinterpret","pos":"v.","def":"to understand something wrongly","cn":"誤解","s":"Many people ________ a cat's slow blink as sleepiness, but it is actually a friendly sign of trust.","zh":"許多人把貓緩慢的眨眼誤解為想睡覺，但它其實是一種表示信任的友善訊號。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B110","t":"誤解"},{"w":"misleading","pos":"adj.","def":"giving the wrong idea","cn":"誤導的","s":"The headline \"Scientists find the gene for intelligence\" was ________, because hundreds of genes affect how we think.","zh":"「科學家找到智力基因」這個標題是誤導的，因為有數百個基因會影響我們如何思考。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B111","t":"誤導的"},{"w":"observational","pos":"adj.","def":"based on watching rather than experiments","cn":"觀察性的","s":"Most of her work is ________, so she spends long hours in the forest and rarely does tests in a lab.","zh":"她大部分的研究是觀察性的，所以她在森林裡待很長的時間，很少在實驗室做測試。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B112","t":"觀察性的"},{"w":"persuasive","pos":"adj.","def":"able to make people believe something","cn":"有說服力的","s":"Darwin's arguments were very ________, because he supported every idea with hundreds of careful examples.","zh":"達爾文的論點非常有說服力，因為他用數百個仔細的例子來支持每一個想法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B113","t":"有說服力"},{"w":"predetermined","pos":"adj.","def":"decided in advance","cn":"預先決定的","s":"Your future is not ________ by your genes, because choices about food, sleep and exercise also matter.","zh":"你的未來並不是由基因預先決定的，因為對飲食、睡眠和運動的選擇也很重要。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B114","t":"預先決定的"},{"w":"provocative","pos":"adj.","def":"causing strong reactions or arguments","cn":"引起爭議的；挑釁的","s":"The professor asked a ________ question about designer babies, and the class argued about it for the whole hour.","zh":"教授問了一個關於訂製嬰兒的引起爭議的問題，而全班為此爭論了整整一個小時。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B115","t":"引起爭議的"},{"w":"reproducible","pos":"adj.","def":"able to be repeated with the same results","cn":"可重複驗證的","s":"Good results should be ________, so other labs must get the same answer when they repeat the test.","zh":"好的研究結果應該是可重複驗證的，所以其他實驗室重做測試時必須得到相同的答案。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B116","t":"可重複驗證的"},{"w":"spurious","pos":"adj.","def":"false, although it seems true","cn":"虛假的；似是而非的","s":"The link between ice cream sales and shark attacks is ________, because both simply increase in hot weather.","zh":"冰淇淋銷量和鯊魚攻擊之間的關聯是似是而非的，因為兩者只是都在炎熱天氣時增加。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B117","t":"似是而非的"},{"w":"unambiguous","pos":"adj.","def":"clear, with only one meaning","cn":"明確的","s":"The bee's dance sends an ________ message, so the other bees fly straight to the right flowers.","zh":"蜜蜂的舞蹈傳達出明確的訊息，所以其他蜜蜂會直接飛往正確的花朵。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B118","t":"明確的"},{"w":"undisputed","pos":"adj.","def":"accepted by everyone","cn":"無可爭議的","s":"The lion is the ________ leader of the group, but younger males may challenge him when he grows old.","zh":"這隻獅子是群體中無可爭議的首領，但當他變老時年輕的雄獅可能會挑戰他。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B119","t":"無可爭議的"},{"w":"unsubstantiated","pos":"adj.","def":"not supported by evidence","cn":"未經證實的","s":"The claim that the pill makes children smarter is ________, so parents should not waste their money on it.","zh":"那種藥丸能讓孩子變聰明的說法是未經證實的，所以父母不應該把錢浪費在上面。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B120","t":"未經證實的"},{"w":"untested","pos":"adj.","def":"not yet tried or checked","cn":"未經測試的","s":"The new treatment is still ________ on humans, so doctors cannot promise that it will be safe.","zh":"這種新療法在人類身上仍未經測試，所以醫生無法保證它是安全的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B121","t":"未經測試"},{"w":"well-documented","pos":"adj.","def":"recorded clearly in many reports","cn":"有充分記錄的","s":"The friendship between elephants is ________, and many videos show them helping each other in trouble.","zh":"大象之間的友誼是有充分記錄的，而許多影片顯示牠們在困境中互相幫助。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B122","t":"有充分記錄的"},{"w":"continuum","pos":"n.","def":"a range where things change gradually","cn":"連續體；連續的範圍","s":"Intelligence is not a simple yes or no, because animals lie along a ________ from simple to very clever.","zh":"智力並不是簡單的有或沒有，因為動物分布在從簡單到非常聰明的連續的範圍上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B123","t":"連續的範圍"},{"w":"counterexample","pos":"n.","def":"an example that shows a rule is not always true","cn":"反例","s":"The teacher said all mammals give birth to live young, but a student gave the platypus as a ________.","zh":"老師說所有哺乳類動物都是胎生的，但一位學生舉出鴨嘴獸作為反例。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B124","t":"反例"},{"w":"experimentation","pos":"n.","def":"the process of trying new ideas in tests","cn":"實驗","s":"After years of ________, the team found a safe way to grow skin in the lab, and burn patients now benefit.","zh":"經過多年的實驗，研究團隊找到了在實驗室中安全培養皮膚的方法，而燒燙傷病人如今因此受益。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B125","t":"實驗"},{"w":"observer","pos":"n.","def":"a person who watches something carefully","cn":"觀察者","s":"A careful ________ will notice that each crow has a slightly different call, so you can tell them apart.","zh":"一位細心的觀察者會注意到每隻烏鴉的叫聲都略有不同，所以你可以分辨牠們。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B126","t":"觀察者"},{"w":"proposal","pos":"n.","def":"a plan or idea that is suggested","cn":"提案；提議","s":"The government rejected the ________ to edit the genes of mosquitoes, because many citizens were worried.","zh":"政府否決了編輯蚊子基因的提案，因為許多市民感到擔憂。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B127","t":"提案"},{"w":"query","pos":"n.","def":"a question","cn":"疑問；詢問","s":"If you have a ________ about your DNA test results, you can email the company, and a genetic adviser will reply.","zh":"如果你對DNA檢測結果有疑問，可以寫電子郵件給公司，而一位遺傳顧問會回覆你。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B128","t":"疑問"},{"w":"supposition","pos":"n.","def":"an idea that is believed without proof","cn":"推測；假定","s":"The idea that dinosaurs were grey was only a ________, but new fossils show that some had colourful feathers.","zh":"恐龍是灰色的這個想法只是推測，但新的化石顯示有些恐龍有色彩繽紛的羽毛。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B129","t":"推測"},{"w":"subject","pos":"n.","def":"a person or animal used in a study","cn":"受試者；研究對象","s":"Each ________ in the study wore a sleep tracker, and the scientists compared their results with their genes.","zh":"研究中的每位受試者都戴著睡眠追蹤器，而科學家把他們的結果和基因作比較。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B130","t":"受試者"},{"w":"fluke","pos":"n.","def":"a lucky or unusual result that happens by chance","cn":"僥倖；偶然","s":"At first, the scientists thought the clever bird was a ________, but other birds soon learned the same trick.","zh":"起初科學家認為那隻聰明的鳥只是偶然，但其他鳥很快也學會了同樣的把戲。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B131","t":"偶然"},{"w":"abnormality","pos":"n.","def":"something that is not usual, often a health problem","cn":"異常","s":"The scan showed a small ________ in the baby's heart, but the doctor said it would probably heal by itself.","zh":"掃描顯示寶寶的心臟有一個小異常，但醫生說它可能會自行癒合。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B132","t":"異常"},{"w":"agent","pos":"n.","def":"something that causes an effect","cn":"媒介；作用物","s":"Mosquitoes are the main ________ that spreads the disease, so the town cleaned all the standing water.","zh":"蚊子是傳播這種疾病的主要媒介，所以這個城鎮清除了所有的積水。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B133","t":"媒介"},{"w":"aggression","pos":"n.","def":"angry or violent behaviour","cn":"攻擊性","s":"Male birds show more ________ in spring, because they must protect their area from other males.","zh":"雄鳥在春天表現出更強的攻擊性，因為牠們必須保護自己的地盤不受其他雄鳥侵犯。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B134","t":"攻擊性"},{"w":"behavioural","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to how a person or animal acts","cn":"行為的","s":"The dog had several ________ problems, so the family hired a trainer to help it feel calm.","zh":"那隻狗有幾個行為的問題，所以這家人請了一位訓練師幫助牠平靜下來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B135","t":"行為的"},{"w":"biologically","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way relating to living things","cn":"生物學上","s":"Humans are ________ very similar to chimps, but our language and culture make us very different.","zh":"人類在生物學上和黑猩猩非常相似，但我們的語言和文化讓我們非常不同。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B136","t":"生物學上"},{"w":"certainty","pos":"n.","def":"the state of being completely sure","cn":"確定性；把握","s":"Scientists cannot say with ________ why the dinosaurs had feathers, but warmth and display are likely reasons.","zh":"科學家無法確定恐龍為什麼有羽毛，但保暖和展示可能是原因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B137","t":"確定"},{"w":"commonly","pos":"adv.","def":"usually or by many people","cn":"普遍地；通常","s":"The fruit fly is ________ used in genetics labs, because it is cheap and breeds every two weeks.","zh":"果蠅普遍地被用於遺傳學實驗室，因為牠便宜而且每兩週就繁殖一次。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B138","t":"普遍地"},{"w":"consciousness","pos":"n.","def":"being awake and aware of yourself","cn":"意識","s":"Scientists still argue about animal ________, but most agree that dogs and apes have feelings.","zh":"科學家仍在爭論動物的意識，但大多數人同意狗和猿類有情感。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B139","t":"意識"},{"w":"descriptive","pos":"adj.","def":"describing what something is like","cn":"描述性的","s":"Her first report was mainly ________, so it explained what the monkeys did but not why they did it.","zh":"她的第一份報告主要是描述性的，所以它解釋了猴子做了什麼，但沒有解釋為什麼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B140","t":"描述性的"},{"w":"detection","pos":"n.","def":"the act of finding or noticing something","cn":"偵測；發現","s":"Early ________ of a genetic disease can help a baby, because doctors can start treatment right away.","zh":"遺傳疾病的早期發現能幫助嬰兒，因為醫生可以立即開始治療。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B141","t":"發現"},{"w":"diagnostic","pos":"adj.","def":"used to find out what illness someone has","cn":"診斷的","s":"The hospital bought new ________ equipment, so patients no longer wait weeks for their test results.","zh":"醫院購買了新的診斷的設備，所以病人不再需要等好幾週才拿到檢查結果。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B142","t":"診斷的"},{"w":"effectively","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that works well","cn":"有效地","s":"The new drug works ________ against the virus, but it is still too expensive for many patients.","zh":"這種新藥能有效地對抗病毒，但對許多病人來說仍然太貴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B143","t":"有效地"},{"w":"efficient","pos":"adj.","def":"working well without wasting time or energy","cn":"有效率的","s":"Penguins are very ________ swimmers, so they can travel long distances while using little energy.","zh":"企鵝是非常有效率的泳者，所以牠們能消耗很少的能量游很長的距離。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B144","t":"有效率的"},{"w":"entirely","pos":"adv.","def":"completely","cn":"完全地","s":"Koalas eat almost ________ eucalyptus leaves, so they cannot survive where those trees do not grow.","zh":"無尾熊幾乎完全以尤加利樹葉為食，所以牠們無法在沒有這種樹的地方生存。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B145","t":"完全"},{"w":"environmental","pos":"adj.","def":"relating to the natural world and surroundings","cn":"環境的","s":"Some illnesses come from genes, but others are caused by ________ factors like dirty air.","zh":"有些疾病來自基因，但其他疾病是由像髒空氣這樣的環境的因素所造成的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B146","t":"環境的"},{"w":"equally","pos":"adv.","def":"to the same degree","cn":"同樣地；平等地","s":"The mother and father penguins share the work ________, and they take turns keeping the egg warm.","zh":"企鵝爸爸和媽媽平等地分擔工作，而且牠們輪流讓蛋保持溫暖。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B147","t":"平等地"},{"w":"existence","pos":"n.","def":"the state of being real or alive","cn":"存在","s":"Scientists doubted the ________ of the giant squid for years, until someone finally filmed one in 2004.","zh":"科學家多年來一直懷疑大王魷的存在，直到2004年終於有人拍到了一隻。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B148","t":"存在"},{"w":"fascinating","pos":"adj.","def":"extremely interesting","cn":"迷人的；極有趣的","s":"The way birds find their way home is ________, and scientists are still not sure how they do it.","zh":"鳥類找到回家路的方式是極有趣的，而科學家仍然不確定牠們是怎麼做到的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B149","t":"極有趣的"},{"w":"gradually","pos":"adv.","def":"slowly over time","cn":"逐漸地","s":"The puppy ________ learned to trust the new family, and after a month it slept happily on the sofa.","zh":"那隻小狗逐漸地學會信任新家人，而一個月後牠快樂地睡在沙發上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B150","t":"逐漸地"},{"w":"imprecise","pos":"adj.","def":"not exact","cn":"不精確的","s":"Early DNA tests were ________, so they sometimes gave the wrong answer about a person's family.","zh":"早期的DNA檢測是不精確的，所以有時會對一個人的家族給出錯誤的答案。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B151","t":"不精確的"},{"w":"ineffective","pos":"adj.","def":"not producing the result you want","cn":"無效的","s":"The old medicine became ________ against the germs, so doctors had to find a new one.","zh":"舊藥對這些病菌變得無效，所以醫生必須找到新的藥。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B152","t":"無效"},{"w":"instinctive","pos":"adj.","def":"done naturally without learning","cn":"本能的","s":"Swimming is ________ for baby ducks, so they follow their mother into the water on their first day.","zh":"游泳對小鴨來說是本能的，所以牠們在出生第一天就跟著媽媽下水。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B153","t":"本能的"},{"w":"intelligent","pos":"adj.","def":"clever and able to learn quickly","cn":"聰明的","s":"Octopuses are very ________ animals, and some have escaped from their tanks by opening the lids.","zh":"章魚是非常聰明的動物，而有些章魚曾經打開蓋子從水族箱裡逃脫。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B154","t":"聰明的"},{"w":"limited","pos":"adj.","def":"small in amount or number","cn":"有限的","s":"Pandas have a ________ diet of bamboo, so they must eat for up to fourteen hours a day.","zh":"熊貓只吃竹子，飲食有限，所以牠們一天必須進食長達十四個小時。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B155","t":"有限"},{"w":"misunderstanding","pos":"n.","def":"a failure to understand correctly","cn":"誤會；誤解","s":"There is a common ________ that humans came from monkeys, but in fact we share an ancestor with them.","zh":"有一個常見的誤解是人類是從猴子變來的，但事實上我們和牠們有共同的祖先。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B156","t":"誤解"},{"w":"originally","pos":"adv.","def":"at first","cn":"起初；原本","s":"Dogs were ________ wild wolves, but people tamed them and they slowly became our loyal friends.","zh":"狗原本是野生的狼，但人們馴服了牠們，而牠們慢慢成為我們忠實的朋友。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B157","t":"原本"},{"w":"permanent","pos":"adj.","def":"lasting forever or for a very long time","cn":"永久的","s":"Gene therapy may offer a ________ cure, so patients would not need to take medicine every day.","zh":"基因療法可能提供永久的治癒，所以病人將不需要每天吃藥。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B158","t":"永久的"},{"w":"possibility","pos":"n.","def":"something that might happen or be true","cn":"可能性","s":"There is a ________ that the gene also affects memory, so the scientists plan to test it next year.","zh":"這個基因也有可能性會影響記憶，所以科學家計畫明年進行測試。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B159","t":"可能性"},{"w":"potentially","pos":"adv.","def":"possibly in the future","cn":"潛在地；可能","s":"Gene editing could ________ cure many diseases, but it may also create problems that we cannot yet predict.","zh":"基因編輯可能治癒許多疾病，但它也可能造成我們目前還無法預測的問題。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B160","t":"可能"},{"w":"probable","pos":"adj.","def":"likely to be true or to happen","cn":"很可能的","s":"A cold winter is the most ________ cause of the birds' deaths, but scientists are also testing for disease.","zh":"寒冷的冬天是這些鳥死亡最可能的原因，但科學家也在檢測是否有疾病。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B161","t":"可能的"},{"w":"problematic","pos":"adj.","def":"full of difficulties","cn":"有問題的；棘手的","s":"Keeping dolphins in small tanks is ________, because they normally swim long distances every day.","zh":"把海豚養在小水族箱裡是有問題的，因為牠們通常每天都游很遠的距離。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B162","t":"有問題的"},{"w":"purposeful","pos":"adj.","def":"done with a clear aim","cn":"有目的的","s":"The crow's actions looked ________, so the scientists believed it was planning how to get the food.","zh":"那隻烏鴉的行為看起來是有目的的，所以科學家相信牠正在計畫如何拿到食物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B163","t":"有目的的"},{"w":"rarely","pos":"adv.","def":"not often","cn":"很少","s":"Male hamsters ________ help raise their babies, so the mother must do all the work alone.","zh":"雄倉鼠很少幫忙養育寶寶，所以母倉鼠必須獨自完成所有工作。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B164","t":"很少"},{"w":"reactive","pos":"adj.","def":"acting in response to something rather than planning","cn":"反應性的；易起反應的","s":"Some dogs are very ________ to noise, and they bark loudly every time a motorbike passes.","zh":"有些狗對噪音非常易起反應，每當有機車經過時牠們都會大聲吠叫。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B165","t":"易起反應"},{"w":"regardless","pos":"adv.","def":"without being affected by something","cn":"不管；無論如何","s":"The salmon swim upriver ________ of the danger, because they must lay their eggs where they were born.","zh":"鮭魚不管危險都會逆流而上，因為牠們必須在自己出生的地方產卵。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B166","t":"不管"},{"w":"responsive","pos":"adj.","def":"reacting quickly and positively","cn":"反應靈敏的","s":"Babies are very ________ to their mother's voice, and they often stop crying when they hear her.","zh":"嬰兒對媽媽的聲音反應非常靈敏，而且他們聽到媽媽的聲音時常常會停止哭泣。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B167","t":"反應 靈敏"},{"w":"self-evident","pos":"adj.","def":"clear without needing proof","cn":"不言而喻的","s":"It may seem ________ that children look like their parents, but the reasons were a mystery until genetics.","zh":"孩子長得像父母這件事似乎不言而喻，但在遺傳學出現之前，其中的原因一直是個謎。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B168","t":"不言而喻"},{"w":"situational","pos":"adj.","def":"depending on the situation","cn":"視情況而定的","s":"The monkey's behaviour was ________, because it acted bravely with friends but hid when it was alone.","zh":"那隻猴子的行為是視情況而定的，因為牠和朋友在一起時很勇敢，但獨自一隻時就躲起來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B169","t":"視情況而定的"},{"w":"socially","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that relates to living in groups","cn":"社交上","s":"Wolves are ________ complex animals, so a lonely wolf often tries hard to find or form a new pack.","zh":"狼在社交上是複雜的動物，所以一隻孤狼常常會努力尋找或組成新的狼群。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B170","t":"社交上"},{"w":"suitable","pos":"adj.","def":"right for a purpose","cn":"合適的","s":"The beach was no longer ________ for nesting, because hotels had been built along the sand.","zh":"這片海灘已不再適合築巢，因為沙灘沿岸已經蓋了飯店。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B171","t":"適合"},{"w":"supportive","pos":"adj.","def":"giving help and encouragement","cn":"支持的","s":"Elephants are very ________ of each other, and they gently touch a stressed friend with their trunks.","zh":"大象之間非常支持彼此，而牠們會用象鼻輕輕觸碰感到緊張的同伴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B172","t":"支持"},{"w":"surprisingly","pos":"adv.","def":"in an unexpected way","cn":"令人驚訝地","s":"Pigs are ________ clever, and some can learn to play simple video games with a joystick.","zh":"豬令人驚訝地聰明，而有些豬能學會用搖桿玩簡單的電玩遊戲。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B173","t":"令人驚訝地"},{"w":"systemic","pos":"adj.","def":"affecting the whole body or system","cn":"全身性的；系統性的","s":"The infection became ________, so it spread through the patient's blood and needed stronger treatment.","zh":"感染變成了全身性的，所以它擴散到病人的血液中，需要更強的治療。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B174","t":"全身性的"},{"w":"territorial","pos":"adj.","def":"defending an area from others","cn":"有領域性的","s":"Robins are very ________ birds, and they will even attack their own reflection in a window.","zh":"知更鳥是非常有領域性的鳥類，而牠們甚至會攻擊自己在窗戶上的倒影。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B175","t":"有領域性的"},{"w":"uncommon","pos":"adj.","def":"not happening often","cn":"不常見的","s":"White tigers are ________ in the wild, because they need a rare gene from both parents.","zh":"白老虎在野外是不常見的，因為牠們需要從父母雙方都得到一個罕見的基因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B176","t":"不常見的"},{"w":"unexpected","pos":"adj.","def":"surprising and not planned","cn":"出乎意料的","s":"The results were ________, because the \"lazy\" ants actually acted as a back-up team when others were lost.","zh":"結果是出乎意料的，因為那些「懶惰」的螞蟻在其他螞蟻消失時其實擔任了後備隊伍。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B177","t":"出乎意料的"},{"w":"unexplained","pos":"adj.","def":"without a known reason","cn":"無法解釋的","s":"Some whales beach themselves for ________ reasons, and scientists are studying whether noise may be the cause.","zh":"有些鯨魚因為無法解釋的原因擱淺，而科學家正在研究噪音是否可能是原因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B178","t":"無法解釋的"},{"w":"unusual","pos":"adj.","def":"different from what is normal","cn":"不尋常的","s":"It is ________ for a male fish to carry eggs, but male seahorses carry their babies in a special pouch.","zh":"雄魚攜帶卵是不尋常的，但雄海馬會把寶寶放在一個特別的育兒袋裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B179","t":"不尋常的"},{"w":"valuable","pos":"adj.","def":"very useful or important","cn":"有價值的；寶貴的","s":"Old museum specimens are ________ to scientists, because their DNA shows how species have changed.","zh":"博物館的舊標本對科學家很寶貴，因為它們的DNA顯示了物種是如何改變的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B180","t":"寶貴"},{"w":"antagonistic","pos":"adj.","def":"showing strong opposition","cn":"敵對的","s":"The two male cats were ________ towards each other, so the owner kept them in separate rooms.","zh":"那兩隻公貓彼此敵對，所以主人把牠們分開養在不同的房間。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B181","t":"敵對"},{"w":"attuned","pos":"adj.","def":"able to understand and react to something","cn":"適應的；熟悉的","s":"Dogs are closely ________ to human faces, and they can often tell when their owner is sad.","zh":"狗對人類的臉部表情非常熟悉，而且牠們常常能察覺主人什麼時候難過。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B182","t":"熟悉"},{"w":"deleterious","pos":"adj.","def":"causing harm","cn":"有害的","s":"Most mutations are ________ or have no effect, but a few help the animal survive.","zh":"大多數突變是有害的或沒有影響，但少數會幫助動物生存。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B183","t":"有害的"},{"w":"docile","pos":"adj.","def":"calm and easy to control","cn":"溫馴的","s":"Farm animals became more ________ over many generations, because farmers kept the calmest ones for breeding.","zh":"農場動物經過許多世代變得更溫馴，因為農民保留最溫和的個體來繁殖。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B184","t":"溫馴"},{"w":"emblematic","pos":"adj.","def":"being a typical symbol of something","cn":"象徵性的；具代表性的","s":"The panda is ________ of animal protection, and its picture appears on many conservation posters.","zh":"熊貓是動物保護的象徵，而牠的圖片出現在許多保育海報上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B185","t":"象徵"},{"w":"gregarious","pos":"adj.","def":"liking to be with others","cn":"群居的；愛交際的","s":"Sheep are ________ animals, so a sheep that is kept alone often becomes stressed and stops eating.","zh":"羊是群居的動物，所以被單獨飼養的羊常常會感到壓力並停止進食。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B186","t":"群居的"},{"w":"intractable","pos":"adj.","def":"very difficult to solve or control","cn":"棘手的；難處理的","s":"The problem of rats on the island seemed ________, but a careful plan finally removed them all.","zh":"島上的鼠患問題似乎很棘手，但一項周密的計畫最終把牠們全部清除了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B187","t":"棘手"},{"w":"placid","pos":"adj.","def":"calm and not easily upset","cn":"平靜的；溫和的","s":"The old horse was ________ and gentle, so the riding school used it for young children.","zh":"那匹老馬溫和而溫順，所以騎馬學校讓牠給年幼的孩子騎。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B188","t":"溫和"},{"w":"proclivity","pos":"n.","def":"a natural tendency to do something","cn":"傾向；癖好","s":"Border collies have a strong ________ for herding, and they may even try to gather children together.","zh":"邊境牧羊犬有強烈的放牧傾向，而牠們甚至可能會試圖把孩子們聚集在一起。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B189","t":"傾向"},{"w":"reclusive","pos":"adj.","def":"avoiding others and living alone","cn":"隱居的；不喜交際的","s":"The snow leopard is a ________ animal, so few people have ever seen one in the wild.","zh":"雪豹是一種不喜交際的動物，所以很少有人曾在野外看過牠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B190","t":"不喜交際的"},{"w":"serendipity","pos":"n.","def":"finding something good by chance","cn":"意外的好運；機緣巧合","s":"Many great discoveries came from ________, because scientists noticed something strange and decided to study it.","zh":"許多偉大的發現來自機緣巧合，因為科學家注意到奇怪的事情並決定研究它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B191","t":"機緣巧合"},{"w":"submissive","pos":"adj.","def":"willing to obey others","cn":"順從的","s":"The young wolf showed ________ behaviour by lying on its back, and the leader stopped growling.","zh":"那隻年輕的狼仰躺著表現出順從的行為，而首領就停止了低吼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B192","t":"順從的"},{"w":"timid","pos":"adj.","def":"shy and easily frightened","cn":"膽小的","s":"The rescued dog was ________ at first, but it slowly became braver with daily walks and kind words.","zh":"那隻被救援的狗起初很膽小，但隨著每天散步和溫柔的話語，牠慢慢變得勇敢。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B193","t":"膽小"},{"w":"observant","pos":"adj.","def":"good at noticing things","cn":"觀察力敏銳的","s":"An ________ student noticed that the ants always took the same path, so she drew a map of their route.","zh":"一位觀察力敏銳的學生注意到螞蟻總是走同一條路，所以她畫了一張牠們路線的地圖。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B194","t":"觀察力敏銳的"},{"w":"alert","pos":"adj.","def":"quick to notice danger","cn":"警覺的","s":"Deer stay ________ while they eat, and they lift their heads every few seconds to listen for wolves.","zh":"鹿在進食時保持警覺，而且牠們每隔幾秒就抬起頭來聆聽狼的動靜。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B195","t":"警覺"},{"w":"defensive","pos":"adj.","def":"protecting yourself from attack","cn":"防禦性的","s":"The mother bear became ________ when we walked near her cubs, so the guide told us to back away slowly.","zh":"當我們走近她的小熊時，母熊變得具防禦性，所以導遊要我們慢慢後退。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B196","t":"防禦性"},{"w":"nimble","pos":"adj.","def":"able to move quickly and lightly","cn":"敏捷的","s":"Mountain goats are very ________ climbers, and they can stand on rocks that look too small for their feet.","zh":"山羊是非常敏捷的攀爬者，而且牠們能站在看起來比牠們的蹄還小的岩石上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B197","t":"敏捷的"},{"w":"showy","pos":"adj.","def":"bright and designed to attract attention","cn":"華麗的；引人注目的","s":"The male bird has ________ feathers, while the female is plain brown so she can hide on the nest.","zh":"雄鳥有華麗的羽毛，而雌鳥是樸素的褐色，好讓她能躲在巢裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B198","t":"華麗的"},{"w":"risky","pos":"adj.","def":"possibly dangerous","cn":"有風險的","s":"Leaving the group is ________ for a young zebra, because lions often attack animals that are alone.","zh":"離開群體對年輕的斑馬來說是有風險的，因為獅子常常攻擊落單的動物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B199","t":"有風險的"},{"w":"harmless","pos":"adj.","def":"not able to cause harm","cn":"無害的","s":"Most spiders in Taiwan are ________ to people, but many children are still afraid of them.","zh":"台灣大多數蜘蛛對人類是無害的，但許多孩子仍然害怕牠們。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B200","t":"無害的"},{"w":"survival of the fittest","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the idea that the best-suited living things survive","cn":"適者生存","s":"Some people use \"______ ______ ______ ______\" to describe business, but Darwin meant fitting the environment, not being the strongest.","zh":"有些人用「適者生存」來形容商業競爭，但達爾文的意思是適應環境，而不是最強壯。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P1","t":"適者生存"},{"w":"run in the family","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to be common among members of one family","cn":"家族遺傳","s":"Musical talent seems to ______ ______ ______ ______, because my grandfather, my mother and my brother all play the piano.","zh":"音樂天分似乎是家族遺傳，因為我的外公、我媽媽和我哥哥都會彈鋼琴。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P2","t":"家族遺傳"},{"w":"birds of a feather flock together","pos":"phr.","def":"people who are alike spend time together","cn":"物以類聚","s":"Tom and his friends all love insects and spend weekends looking for beetles, so ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"湯姆和他的朋友們都熱愛昆蟲，週末都在找甲蟲，所以真是物以類聚。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P3","t":"物以類聚"},{"w":"like father, like son","pos":"phr.","def":"a son is often similar to his father","cn":"有其父必有其子","s":"My dad laughs exactly the way my brother does, and my grandmother always smiles and says, \"______ ______, ______ ______.\"","zh":"我爸爸笑起來跟我哥哥一模一樣，而我奶奶總是微笑著說：「有其父必有其子。」","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P4","t":"有其父必有其子"},{"w":"the apple doesn't fall far from the tree","pos":"phr.","def":"children are often like their parents","cn":"有其父母必有其子女","s":"Her mother was a famous scientist, and now she is studying genes too, so ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"她的母親是一位著名的科學家，而現在她也在研究基因，所以真是有其父母必有其子女。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P5","t":"有其父母必有其子女"},{"w":"a chip off the old block","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a person who is very similar to a parent","cn":"酷似父母的孩子","s":"Kevin is as funny and talkative as his father, and everyone at the party said he was ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"凱文和他爸爸一樣風趣又健談，而派對上每個人都說他酷似他爸爸。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P6","t":"酷似他爸爸"},{"w":"in one's genes","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"natural to someone because of their family","cn":"天生的；與生俱來的","s":"Running seems to be ______ ______ ______, because her parents were both Olympic athletes and she won her first race at six.","zh":"跑步似乎是她與生俱來的能力，因為她的父母都是奧運選手，而她六歲就贏得了第一場比賽。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P7","t":"與生俱來的"},{"w":"pass on","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to give something to children or the next generation","cn":"傳給；遺傳給","s":"Parents can ______ ______ certain illnesses to their children, so doctors sometimes suggest a gene test before pregnancy.","zh":"父母可能會把某些疾病遺傳給孩子，所以醫生有時會建議在懷孕前做基因檢測。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P8","t":"遺傳給"},{"w":"take after","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to look or behave like an older family member","cn":"長得像；性格像（長輩）","s":"I ______ ______ my grandmother, because we both have green eyes and we both love gardening.","zh":"我長得像我奶奶，因為我們都有綠色的眼睛，而且都熱愛園藝。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P9","t":"長得像"},{"w":"the early bird catches the worm","pos":"phr.","def":"people who start early will succeed","cn":"早起的鳥兒有蟲吃","s":"My mum always wakes me at six before exams, because she believes ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"考試前我媽媽總是六點叫我起床，因為她相信早起的鳥兒有蟲吃。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P10","t":"早起的鳥兒有蟲吃"},{"w":"a leopard can't change its spots","pos":"phr.","def":"people cannot change their basic character","cn":"本性難移","s":"He promised to stop being late, but he was late again the next day, so ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"他答應不再遲到，但隔天又遲到了，所以真是本性難移。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P11","t":"本性難移"},{"w":"cry wolf","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to give a false warning so people stop believing you","cn":"謊報危險；放羊的孩子","s":"If you ______ ______ too often about being sick, your teacher may not believe you when you really feel ill.","zh":"如果你太常謊報生病，當你真的不舒服時老師可能不會相信你。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P12","t":"謊報"},{"w":"let the cat out of the bag","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to tell a secret by mistake","cn":"洩露祕密","s":"We planned a surprise party for Mum, but my little sister ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, so the surprise was ruined.","zh":"我們為媽媽計畫了一場驚喜派對，但我妹妹洩露了祕密，所以驚喜就泡湯了。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P13","t":"洩露了祕密"},{"w":"the black sheep of the family","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a family member who is different or disapproved of","cn":"家族中的害群之馬；異類","s":"Everyone in my family became a doctor, but my uncle became a rock singer, so he calls himself ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______.","zh":"我家每個人都成了醫生，但我叔叔成了搖滾歌手，所以他自稱是家族中的異類。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P14","t":"家族中的異類"},{"w":"the lion's share","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the largest part of something","cn":"最大的一份","s":"The dominant wolf usually takes ______ ______ ______ of the food, while the younger wolves wait for what is left.","zh":"地位最高的狼通常拿走食物中最大的一份，而年輕的狼則等著吃剩下的。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P15","t":"最大的一份"},{"w":"you can't teach an old dog new tricks","pos":"phr.","def":"it is hard to change old habits","cn":"老狗學不會新把戲；積習難改","s":"My grandfather refuses to use a smartphone and says ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, but I am still trying to teach him.","zh":"我爺爺拒絕使用智慧型手機，還說老狗學不會新把戲，但我仍在努力教他。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P16","t":"老狗學不會新把戲"},{"w":"monkey see, monkey do","pos":"phr.","def":"people copy what others do without thinking","cn":"有樣學樣","s":"My little brother copies everything I do, so when I started eating vegetables, he did too—______ ______, ______ ______.","zh":"我弟弟什麼都學我，所以當我開始吃蔬菜時，他也跟著吃——真是有樣學樣。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P17","t":"有樣學樣"},{"w":"dog-eat-dog","pos":"adj.","def":"very competitive, where people harm others to succeed","cn":"殘酷競爭的；弱肉強食的","s":"Life in the wild is a ________ world, and only the animals that find enough food survive the winter.","zh":"野外的生活是一個弱肉強食的世界，而只有找到足夠食物的動物才能熬過冬天。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P18","t":"弱肉強食的"},{"w":"give rise to","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to cause something to happen or exist","cn":"引起；導致","s":"A small change in one gene can ______ ______ ______ a new feature, and over time that feature may spread through the species.","zh":"一個基因的小改變就能導致一個新特徵的出現，而隨著時間推移，這個特徵可能會擴散到整個物種。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P19","t":"導致"},{"w":"ruffle someone's feathers","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to annoy or upset someone","cn":"惹惱某人","s":"My classmate's rude joke about my drawing ______ ______ ______, but I tried to stay calm and smiled at him.","zh":"我同學對我畫作的無禮玩笑惹惱了我，但我試著保持冷靜並對他微笑。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P20","t":"惹惱了我"}]};
